1
00:00:56,990 --> 00:01:00,228
Here in the upstate,
things don't change much.

4
00:01:00,294 --> 00:01:01,895
Fall means
football season.

5
00:01:01,962 --> 00:01:03,197
Being
married to a coach

6
00:01:03,264 --> 00:01:04,565
means
measuring things...

7
00:01:04,632 --> 00:01:07,000
...mainly by
wins and losses.

8
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:09,703
Except for
that one year.

9
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:11,872
Jimmy Carter declared
that if elected...

10
00:01:11,939 --> 00:01:13,574
...he would do
everything possible

11
00:01:13,641 --> 00:01:15,376
to clean up
the government.

12
00:01:15,443 --> 00:01:17,645
In South Carolina weather,
late night

13
00:01:17,711 --> 00:01:20,013
and early
morning low clouds....

14
00:02:52,306 --> 00:02:53,441
Come on, let's go.

15
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:54,575
No, Mom.

16
00:03:14,528 --> 00:03:17,331
What's wrong with you, boy?!
Get out of my way!

17
00:03:17,765 --> 00:03:19,032
Damn!

18
00:03:49,530 --> 00:03:52,900
Laird, son, how many years
you been playing for me?

19
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:54,268
Two years, coach.

20
00:03:54,335 --> 00:03:55,736
You want to make that three?

21
00:03:55,803 --> 00:03:57,271
I suggest you
start paying attention.

22
00:03:57,338 --> 00:03:59,507
Yes, sir.

23
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:02,510
We do things as a team,
gentlemen.

24
00:04:02,576 --> 00:04:04,712
One player doesn't execute,
it's the

25
00:04:04,778 --> 00:04:07,080
difference between
6 yards or 6 points.

26
00:04:07,147 --> 00:04:11,585
Honeycutt, what say we do
some up-downs as a team...

27
00:04:11,652 --> 00:04:14,221
...so we can
further appreciate
that concept.

28
00:04:14,288 --> 00:04:18,426
You heard the man!
Get them feet chopping now!

29
00:04:18,492 --> 00:04:20,494
Get it up nice!
Get those knees up!

30
00:04:20,561 --> 00:04:22,062
Get them legs going!

31
00:04:23,331 --> 00:04:26,199
Get it up!
Get it up, right now!

32
00:04:44,084 --> 00:04:46,887
Come on, get them up!
Get them up!
Get them up!

33
00:04:50,624 --> 00:04:52,960
Let's go! Come on, now!

34
00:05:10,378 --> 00:05:11,879
Hey, you.

35
00:05:14,214 --> 00:05:17,818
Now, might any of
those X's and O's
be for me tonight?

36
00:05:19,353 --> 00:05:20,888
How's it coming?

37
00:05:20,954 --> 00:05:22,423
Almost done.

38
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,829
Mary Helen home yet?

39
00:05:31,264 --> 00:05:34,101
Mary Helen's been in bed
for an hour, Harold.

40
00:05:36,236 --> 00:05:38,205
Y'all do have
a week before you

41
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:40,340
actually have to
play this game, right?

42
00:05:40,408 --> 00:05:41,775
Right.

43
00:05:41,842 --> 00:05:44,144
I'll be right up.

44
00:05:44,211 --> 00:05:47,915
Ah, the first ''I'll be right up''
of the season.

45
00:05:47,981 --> 00:05:50,117
Ready! Set!

46
00:05:50,584 --> 00:05:52,019
Hut!

47
00:05:52,085 --> 00:05:53,353
Let's go, now.

48
00:05:59,126 --> 00:06:02,796
Team, full speed!
Live to the ball!

49
00:06:08,368 --> 00:06:09,537
Ready!

50
00:06:09,603 --> 00:06:11,772
Blue, 2 4!

51
00:06:12,239 --> 00:06:13,206
Set!

52
00:06:29,089 --> 00:06:31,925
Hey, Einstein. Why don't you try
picking the ball up.

53
00:06:31,992 --> 00:06:34,495
Yeah, you, dummy.
What, you deaf?

54
00:06:34,562 --> 00:06:36,564
Yeah, pick it up.
There you go.

55
00:06:38,098 --> 00:06:39,900
Throw it over here.

56
00:06:41,301 --> 00:06:42,703
Come on, throw it!

57
00:06:47,475 --> 00:06:49,610
What are you doing?
Hey, coach!

58
00:06:50,578 --> 00:06:51,945
He took our ball.

59
00:06:54,782 --> 00:06:55,783
Wha--?

60
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:58,185
Run it again!

61
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,009
See you tomorrow.

62
00:07:22,075 --> 00:07:23,944
Okay.
See you later, Mary Helen.

63
00:07:24,011 --> 00:07:25,212
Bye.

64
00:07:30,951 --> 00:07:32,820
You're getting home late.

65
00:07:32,886 --> 00:07:34,988
Oh, hey, Daddy.

66
00:07:35,055 --> 00:07:38,492
I tried calling a couple times,
but the line was busy.

67
00:07:38,559 --> 00:07:40,127
Your mama's asleep.

68
00:07:40,193 --> 00:07:42,563
I'll talk to her in
the morning, okay?

69
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:44,565
All right.

70
00:07:46,099 --> 00:07:47,467
Night.

71
00:07:47,535 --> 00:07:48,869
Good night.

72
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:55,475
Heard Mary Helen made
varsity cheerleader.

73
00:07:55,543 --> 00:07:56,977
She's really excited.

74
00:07:57,044 --> 00:07:58,546
I'll bet.
I'll bet Linda is too.

75
00:07:58,612 --> 00:08:00,480
Yeah, I guess so.

76
00:08:01,715 --> 00:08:03,050
Do it again!

77
00:08:03,851 --> 00:08:05,318
One more time!

78
00:08:05,385 --> 00:08:06,920
You got them
running something?

79
00:08:06,987 --> 00:08:07,988
Hit it!

80
00:08:09,623 --> 00:08:11,525
Come on, dope.

81
00:08:11,592 --> 00:08:12,960
Hey, boy!

82
00:08:13,026 --> 00:08:14,662
Watch this. Watch this.

83
00:08:17,565 --> 00:08:19,199
Bring them in.

84
00:08:19,266 --> 00:08:21,001
Gather up! On the double!

85
00:08:27,207 --> 00:08:30,678
Well, is someone gonna
tell me what's going on here?

86
00:08:34,815 --> 00:08:36,784
How about it, Johnny?

87
00:08:41,321 --> 00:08:43,023
Nobody move.

88
00:08:43,090 --> 00:08:45,626
On, no, no, no, no.

89
00:08:49,830 --> 00:08:51,398
Oh, gee.

90
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:57,104
I just want to help you.

91
00:08:59,039 --> 00:09:01,408
I'm just gonna cut
the tape off you.

92
00:09:03,944 --> 00:09:07,147
You've gotta hold still.
Just try to hold still, now.

93
00:09:07,214 --> 00:09:09,650
You gotta hold still.
Look at me.

94
00:09:09,717 --> 00:09:11,685
Hold still.
I'm not gonna hurt you.

95
00:09:11,752 --> 00:09:13,921
Hold still.
I don't want to cut you.

96
00:09:15,856 --> 00:09:18,158
My God. It's all right.

97
00:09:18,225 --> 00:09:20,260
Calm down a little bit.
It's okay.

98
00:09:20,327 --> 00:09:24,164
I got it. Gonna get you
out of this mess.

99
00:09:24,231 --> 00:09:25,766
Okay, you're free.

100
00:09:44,918 --> 00:09:46,987
Anybody got anything to say?

101
00:09:51,458 --> 00:09:55,062
Tell your folks practice's gonna
run late tomorrow.

102
00:10:03,036 --> 00:10:06,073
Mary Helen tells me the cheerleading
squad's got itself...

103
00:10:06,139 --> 00:10:08,008
...what,
half-a-dozen new faces

104
00:10:08,075 --> 00:10:10,077
this semester,
isn't that right?

105
00:10:11,344 --> 00:10:13,446
I also hear
the athletic director...

106
00:10:13,513 --> 00:10:16,684
...has to take the top spot
on the pyramid at pep rallies.

107
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:19,019
Isn't that right?

108
00:10:19,086 --> 00:10:21,388
Harold,
why not stop by and see what

109
00:10:21,454 --> 00:10:23,857
kind of no-good
your daughter's up to?

110
00:10:23,924 --> 00:10:25,058
Yeah, sure.

111
00:10:29,196 --> 00:10:31,364
You got a couple
phone calls, Daddy.

112
00:10:32,833 --> 00:10:35,168
From who?

113
00:10:35,235 --> 00:10:38,939
Bobby Taggert's folks.
Frank Clay. I wrote them down for you.

114
00:10:39,807 --> 00:10:41,408
What'd you tell them?

115
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:44,144
That you'd call back.

116
00:10:44,211 --> 00:10:47,748
Have you decided what you're
gonna do about these boys?

117
00:10:47,815 --> 00:10:49,249
Not yet.

118
00:10:50,583 --> 00:10:52,385
I'm sure most of
them have never

119
00:10:52,452 --> 00:10:54,321
done anything
like this before.

120
00:10:54,387 --> 00:10:58,358
You didn't see the look
on this young man's face, Linda.

121
00:10:58,425 --> 00:11:00,260
He was terrified.

122
00:11:14,574 --> 00:11:16,609
Coach Jones?

123
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:18,411
Go on. Good idea.

124
00:11:18,478 --> 00:11:20,613
Might I have
a minute of your time?

125
00:11:21,815 --> 00:11:24,785
Y'all, excuse me.

126
00:11:24,852 --> 00:11:27,755
Anybody ever said no to you on that,
Principal Daniels?

127
00:11:27,821 --> 00:11:29,957
Nobody still working here.

128
00:11:31,591 --> 00:11:33,794
He scores!

129
00:11:33,861 --> 00:11:35,863
What can I do for you?

130
00:11:35,929 --> 00:11:38,531
I hear we had
an incident yesterday.

131
00:11:38,598 --> 00:11:40,667
Yes, ma'am, we did.

132
00:11:40,734 --> 00:11:43,070
You taking care of it?

133
00:11:43,136 --> 00:11:45,338
Let's just say
today's practice won't be

134
00:11:45,405 --> 00:11:47,775
the shortest one
we've ever had.

135
00:11:47,841 --> 00:11:50,510
Good. Good.

136
00:11:50,577 --> 00:11:52,312
You know, Harold...

137
00:11:52,379 --> 00:11:56,349
...that boy has been rolling by here
for a long time now...

138
00:11:56,416 --> 00:11:58,051
...minding his own business.

139
00:11:58,118 --> 00:12:02,422
Never caused any problem
for anybody.

140
00:12:02,489 --> 00:12:04,925
I need you all to
keep it that way.

141
00:12:07,660 --> 00:12:09,162
I appreciate it.

142
00:12:42,963 --> 00:12:45,232
No, I don't want the football.

143
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:51,905
I just want to tell you I'm sorry
about what happened.

144
00:12:51,972 --> 00:12:54,908
I thought you
needed to hear that from someone.

145
00:12:56,543 --> 00:12:58,846
I don't want the football.
You keep it.

146
00:13:00,347 --> 00:13:03,183
Why don't you
bring it by practice later.

147
00:13:03,250 --> 00:13:06,419
I'll find you something to do.
Maybe you can help us out.

148
00:13:11,558 --> 00:13:14,261
Nothing more is
gonna happen, son.

149
00:13:14,327 --> 00:13:15,896
I promise you.

150
00:13:21,601 --> 00:13:24,071
See you later. All right?

151
00:13:46,359 --> 00:13:48,962
All right, the nine of you.

152
00:13:49,029 --> 00:13:50,763
You know who you are.

153
00:13:52,399 --> 00:13:54,101
Get on down there.

154
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:57,504
Take your shoulder pads off.
Line up on the chalk.

155
00:13:57,570 --> 00:13:59,406
Let's go. Hustle up!

156
00:14:01,942 --> 00:14:03,843
Well...

157
00:14:03,911 --> 00:14:05,645
...what do you want to do?

158
00:14:05,712 --> 00:14:07,780
Run them.

159
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:09,149
How long?

160
00:14:11,751 --> 00:14:13,753
Till I say stop.

161
00:14:18,158 --> 00:14:21,061
On the line now!
Where you're going to be.

162
00:14:21,561 --> 00:14:22,562
Ready.

163
00:14:27,667 --> 00:14:29,669
All the way to the line,
coach.

164
00:14:44,551 --> 00:14:47,387
Don't quit on me now!
Don't you quit on me!

165
00:14:47,454 --> 00:14:51,258
All the way through that line!
All the way through!

166
00:15:36,136 --> 00:15:38,105
Hey.
Hi.

167
00:15:44,611 --> 00:15:46,279
Yeah.
Long day?

168
00:15:48,648 --> 00:15:50,183
How was yours?

169
00:15:50,883 --> 00:15:52,085
Long.

170
00:15:54,821 --> 00:15:57,090
So the report is
that Mary Helen

171
00:15:57,157 --> 00:15:59,526
got off to a great
start in lit class...

172
00:15:59,592 --> 00:16:01,628
...but she's
struggling with math.

173
00:16:01,694 --> 00:16:03,663
Well,
the lit part sounds good.

174
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:07,434
Come on, Harold.

175
00:16:07,500 --> 00:16:10,170
It's bad enough when a parent
misses a conference.

176
00:16:10,237 --> 00:16:12,472
It's worse when the parent's
a teacher.

177
00:16:12,539 --> 00:16:15,975
The parent's a teacher,
he knows how his kid's doing.

178
00:16:19,846 --> 00:16:21,781
What?

179
00:16:21,848 --> 00:16:24,817
Please just tell me
that you forgot to go.

180
00:16:24,884 --> 00:16:27,354
You know I had to deal
with those boys.

181
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:29,656
Oh, those boys.

182
00:16:29,722 --> 00:16:32,625
Can't you make room
for your
daughter and those boys?

183
00:16:32,692 --> 00:16:34,894
Don't lecture me.
I'll go see Ms. Marks

184
00:16:34,961 --> 00:16:37,230
tomorrow if it'll
make you feel better.

185
00:16:37,297 --> 00:16:40,733
Make me feel better?
This is not about me.

186
00:16:41,634 --> 00:16:43,270
She's a junior, Harold.

187
00:16:46,106 --> 00:16:50,377
I mean, she's got this year
and next.

188
00:16:50,443 --> 00:16:52,445
And then she's gone.

189
00:17:01,121 --> 00:17:02,422
Go!

190
00:17:05,325 --> 00:17:06,926
Yes, sir!
Y'all ready?

191
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,729
Yes, sir!

192
00:17:09,796 --> 00:17:11,831
Close your eyes for a minute.

193
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:15,302
I want you to listen.

194
00:17:16,269 --> 00:17:18,505
You hear that?

195
00:17:18,571 --> 00:17:20,707
Imagine what
that'Il sound like

196
00:17:20,773 --> 00:17:22,975
after we've all
done our job tonight.

197
00:17:24,511 --> 00:17:25,845
And then...

198
00:17:27,647 --> 00:17:30,750
...I want you to imagine what
that's gonna feel like.

199
00:17:30,817 --> 00:17:34,721
I want you to picture your man
right across from you.

200
00:17:37,457 --> 00:17:39,692
You see him?

201
00:17:39,759 --> 00:17:43,196
You make the effort on every play,
you'll beat them.

202
00:17:43,263 --> 00:17:45,998
You play smart,
you're gonna outthink them.

203
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:48,535
You play with
heart and character...

204
00:17:48,601 --> 00:17:51,704
...and give your teammates everything
you've got on every play...

205
00:17:51,771 --> 00:17:55,475
...you can walk off the field calling
yourselves a football team.

206
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:03,416
Let's play with Hanna pride and never
stop believing in each other.

207
00:18:03,483 --> 00:18:05,618
You win your battles...

208
00:18:05,685 --> 00:18:08,020
...we'll win our war.

209
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:10,823
What's say let's have some fun
and get it done.

210
00:18:13,893 --> 00:18:17,964
Your Hanna
Yellow Jackets!

211
00:18:22,235 --> 00:18:24,437
Let's go, Jackets!

212
00:18:24,504 --> 00:18:26,206
The kickoff is
high and deep...

213
00:18:26,273 --> 00:18:28,107
...and sends
the Jackets' Johnny Clay

214
00:18:28,175 --> 00:18:30,877
back near
the goal line.

215
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:33,146
Johnny Clay behind
a convoy of Hanna

216
00:18:33,213 --> 00:18:35,482
blockers. Heads up
the right sideline.

217
00:18:35,548 --> 00:18:37,450
Go! Go! Go! Go!

218
00:18:37,517 --> 00:18:39,085
Get up there!

219
00:18:39,152 --> 00:18:41,288
Finally knocked out-of-bounds
at the 42-yard line.

220
00:18:41,354 --> 00:18:43,556
Throw right 63 flag. Come on.

221
00:18:43,623 --> 00:18:44,757
Come on!

222
00:18:44,824 --> 00:18:47,026
First and 1 0
for the Jackets.

223
00:18:47,093 --> 00:18:48,628
Marcum back to pass.

224
00:18:48,695 --> 00:18:50,330
Finds Hawkins in
the right flat

225
00:18:50,397 --> 00:18:52,131
for another
Jacket first down.

226
00:18:52,199 --> 00:18:54,934
Get over here.
Come on. Come on.

227
00:18:55,001 --> 00:18:56,836
Thirty-six crossbuck.

228
00:18:56,903 --> 00:18:58,838
Once you get the ball,
I don't wanna

229
00:18:58,905 --> 00:19:00,907
see nothing but
the back of your jersey.

230
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:02,775
All right. Get out there.

231
00:19:03,876 --> 00:19:05,345
The handoff is to Clay.

232
00:19:05,412 --> 00:19:07,480
Finds a big hole.
Now cuts outside.

233
00:19:07,547 --> 00:19:09,682
Beats one tackler.
And another.

234
00:19:09,749 --> 00:19:11,584
Get upfield, son. Turn it on!

235
00:19:11,651 --> 00:19:13,553
He may go all the way.

236
00:19:14,654 --> 00:19:15,688
Touchdown, Hanna!

237
00:19:15,755 --> 00:19:17,123
Yeah! All right.

238
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:19,659
Johnny Clay
with a 30-yard run

239
00:19:19,726 --> 00:19:21,528
gives
the Jackets the lead!

240
00:19:21,594 --> 00:19:23,029
Less than two
minutes to play.

241
00:19:23,095 --> 00:19:24,597
That's what we want.

242
00:19:28,301 --> 00:19:30,002
That's a 30-yard run, son!

243
00:19:32,339 --> 00:19:34,941
That's our ball game!
That's our ball game!

244
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,932
Hey, coach.
Evening, fellas.

245
00:19:59,999 --> 00:20:01,801
Honeycutt.
Harold.

246
00:20:01,868 --> 00:20:03,336
Del. Don.

247
00:20:04,437 --> 00:20:05,938
Kurt. Dennis.

248
00:20:06,005 --> 00:20:08,040
Just brewed that
pot 1 0 minutes ago,

249
00:20:08,107 --> 00:20:10,176
coach.
Got yourself the first cup.

250
00:20:10,243 --> 00:20:11,478
All right.

251
00:20:18,084 --> 00:20:19,085
Well...

252
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,155
...didn't
exactly thump them...

253
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:27,159
...but it wasn't too bad
as far as season openers go.

254
00:20:27,226 --> 00:20:29,862
Frank, your boy, Johnny,
had a heck of a run.

255
00:20:29,929 --> 00:20:32,699
Give him the ball,
he'll make you a smart man.

256
00:20:32,765 --> 00:20:33,933
That's right.

257
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,036
Did notice a few things
we need to work on.

258
00:20:37,103 --> 00:20:40,607
You reckon these are the boys
gonna take us back to state?

259
00:20:40,673 --> 00:20:44,243
Come on, Clive. Little early
for that kind of talk, isn't it?

260
00:20:44,311 --> 00:20:47,514
I hear Easley has a pretty
decent crop of speed this year.

261
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:50,149
I guess we'll see about that
next week.

262
00:20:50,216 --> 00:20:52,919
Think you might want to throw
the ball a bit more?

263
00:20:52,985 --> 00:20:54,754
I think about a lot of things.

264
00:20:54,821 --> 00:20:57,390
Listen, boys.
Last thing coach needs

265
00:20:57,457 --> 00:21:00,126
is us asking him
a slew of questions.

266
00:21:00,192 --> 00:21:03,730
Especially after how he got
those young men to play.

267
00:21:03,796 --> 00:21:05,765
We got them
revved up, didn't we?

268
00:21:05,832 --> 00:21:09,035
So how do you plan on beating those
Easley boys Friday night?

269
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:12,405
Well, Frank, if I was to tell you
that...

270
00:21:12,472 --> 00:21:15,442
...y'all wouldn't have a thing to talk
about all week.

271
00:21:21,814 --> 00:21:24,183
Boy, that's a good
cup tonight, Del.

272
00:21:24,250 --> 00:21:25,452
Thank you.

273
00:21:27,086 --> 00:21:29,922
Come on, turn it up!
Turn it up!
Turn it up!

274
00:21:30,823 --> 00:21:33,760
Good job! Good job!

275
00:21:40,867 --> 00:21:42,935
Hey, Honeycutt.

276
00:21:43,002 --> 00:21:44,236
Yeah?

277
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:46,238
See that young man over there?

278
00:21:47,407 --> 00:21:49,709
What do you figure he wants?

279
00:21:49,776 --> 00:21:50,943
I don't know.

280
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:53,880
Come on, Spaulding,
bring it around there!

281
00:21:53,946 --> 00:21:55,848
I think maybe he's thirsty.

282
00:22:01,654 --> 00:22:03,322
Well, go on.

283
00:22:10,930 --> 00:22:12,699
All right. Five minutes.

284
00:22:12,765 --> 00:22:15,435
Get yourself a drink.
Get on special teams.

285
00:22:21,641 --> 00:22:23,175
How you doing?

286
00:22:23,242 --> 00:22:26,713
Yeah, you. No, wait, wait.
It's all right.

287
00:22:26,779 --> 00:22:29,215
Settle down. I ain't gonna
give you a hug.

288
00:22:29,281 --> 00:22:32,885
Just got a little water here.
See?

289
00:22:32,952 --> 00:22:35,788
I'm dropping
something off here.

290
00:22:35,855 --> 00:22:38,090
Little something
from Coach Jones.

291
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:40,860
Got a name, son?

292
00:22:43,162 --> 00:22:45,398
You ain't gonna
talk to me, are you?

293
00:22:45,465 --> 00:22:47,299
All right.

294
00:22:47,366 --> 00:22:50,002
Go ahead.
Go on, give it a squeeze.

295
00:22:54,306 --> 00:22:56,142
Set! Hut!

296
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:02,549
Come on, now!

297
00:23:02,615 --> 00:23:03,983
Good job, Justin.

298
00:23:10,890 --> 00:23:12,592
All right, bring it in!

299
00:23:23,069 --> 00:23:24,303
Hi.

300
00:23:27,874 --> 00:23:29,375
Glad you came by.

301
00:23:38,184 --> 00:23:40,687
Thank you. What's your name?

302
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:49,929
Why don't you come on in.

303
00:23:49,996 --> 00:23:53,199
I got some hamburgers coming.

304
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:55,101
Get your buggy. Come on in.

305
00:24:12,919 --> 00:24:14,787
Really good burgers.

306
00:24:42,348 --> 00:24:45,151
Oh, you found some music
you like. Good.

307
00:24:51,558 --> 00:24:53,526
Hey, look who's here.

308
00:24:57,396 --> 00:24:59,331
No ketchup, no onion.

309
00:24:59,398 --> 00:25:00,567
Thank you.

310
00:25:01,834 --> 00:25:03,670
He tell you his name yet?

311
00:25:03,736 --> 00:25:05,805
He doesn't talk too much.

312
00:25:05,872 --> 00:25:08,775
But he's sure taken a liking
to that radio of yours.

313
00:25:10,342 --> 00:25:11,778
Radio.

314
00:25:13,512 --> 00:25:14,881
Radio, huh?

315
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:21,821
You know,
it's just sitting there.

316
00:25:21,888 --> 00:25:24,423
You can have it as far
as I'm concerned.

317
00:25:24,490 --> 00:25:26,025
Hey, you hear that...

318
00:25:26,726 --> 00:25:29,061
...Radio?

319
00:25:29,128 --> 00:25:30,963
Coach Honeycutt
says you can take

320
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:33,299
that home with
you if you like.

321
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:34,867
Hey, are you hungry?

322
00:25:35,768 --> 00:25:37,503
Would you like a hambur--?

323
00:25:43,175 --> 00:25:47,213
You want something to wash it
down with too?
Root beer? Coke?

324
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:49,015
Coke.

325
00:25:52,051 --> 00:25:53,485
Man knows what he wants.

326
00:25:53,552 --> 00:25:54,954
Coke, it is.

327
00:26:21,013 --> 00:26:22,815
Well...

328
00:26:22,882 --> 00:26:25,517
...which way's home, Radio?

329
00:26:50,009 --> 00:26:52,845
There's nothing wrong
with a good country station.

330
00:26:56,348 --> 00:26:58,651
But I can get
used to this too, I guess.

331
00:27:07,059 --> 00:27:09,829
You know, the boys call me
Coach Jones.

332
00:27:11,363 --> 00:27:12,699
Coach Jones.

333
00:27:12,765 --> 00:27:15,668
You can call me what you like
when you get around to it.

334
00:27:16,869 --> 00:27:18,337
All right?

335
00:27:41,227 --> 00:27:43,963
I hope you can
come by practice tomorrow

336
00:27:44,030 --> 00:27:46,699
The same time. All right?

337
00:27:55,674 --> 00:27:57,543
See you then, okay?

338
00:27:59,611 --> 00:28:00,980
Afternoon, ma'am.

339
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:05,918
I'm Harold Jones.I coach the football
team over at Hanna High.

340
00:28:07,887 --> 00:28:10,990
I was just giving your boy
a ride home.

341
00:28:13,659 --> 00:28:15,194
Come on in now, baby.

342
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:39,886
Look.

343
00:28:44,090 --> 00:28:45,324
Hey.

344
00:28:46,058 --> 00:28:47,726
Yeah.
Hello.

345
00:28:47,794 --> 00:28:49,328
Look.

346
00:28:49,395 --> 00:28:51,030
I see you got
yourself another one.

347
00:28:51,097 --> 00:28:52,664
Look.

348
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:55,334
Oh, look at that.

349
00:28:55,401 --> 00:28:57,703
You get that from him?

350
00:28:57,770 --> 00:29:01,107
Yeah. Coach Jones.

351
00:29:04,576 --> 00:29:06,145
Look at that one.

352
00:29:07,980 --> 00:29:09,281
He a nice man?

353
00:29:10,149 --> 00:29:11,617
Yeah.

354
00:29:11,683 --> 00:29:13,452
Good.

355
00:29:13,519 --> 00:29:17,323
I think it's time you got washed up
for dinner. You hungry?

356
00:29:17,389 --> 00:29:19,091
Yeah.

357
00:29:19,158 --> 00:29:20,993
I made you some fried bread.

358
00:29:22,995 --> 00:29:25,865
All right.Get yourself washed up
for dinner.

359
00:29:32,204 --> 00:29:34,106
Set!

360
00:29:34,173 --> 00:29:36,175
Get in there! Get in there!

361
00:29:38,044 --> 00:29:41,313
Bring it in! Come on, hustle up!
Let's go.

362
00:29:41,380 --> 00:29:43,816
Come on, hustle up!

363
00:29:43,883 --> 00:29:47,486
Bring it in.
Good job. Good job.
Good practice, men.

364
00:29:47,553 --> 00:29:49,822
We got a lot to
think about this week.

365
00:29:49,889 --> 00:29:52,791
Easley's got a ton of speed.

366
00:29:52,859 --> 00:29:57,529
Defense, containment. We gotta
keep them from
getting outside.

367
00:29:57,596 --> 00:29:59,698
Offense, ball control.
We'll grind it

368
00:29:59,765 --> 00:30:02,034
out, keep their
offense off the field.

369
00:30:03,502 --> 00:30:05,771
Now, there's one other thing.

370
00:30:05,838 --> 00:30:08,707
See the young man over there?

371
00:30:08,774 --> 00:30:12,979
Believe some of you already
know him. He goes by Radio.

372
00:30:13,045 --> 00:30:15,214
He'll be helping
us out for a while.

373
00:30:17,783 --> 00:30:19,986
We will not have
a problem with that.

374
00:30:20,052 --> 00:30:21,687
No, sir.

375
00:30:22,955 --> 00:30:24,356
Call it up, Danny.

376
00:30:28,627 --> 00:30:29,962
One, two, three!

377
00:30:30,029 --> 00:30:31,330
Beat Easley!

378
00:30:38,037 --> 00:30:40,006
What's he doing?

379
00:30:40,072 --> 00:30:42,008
That's it. Get your knees up.

380
00:30:43,109 --> 00:30:45,144
Look at him out there.

381
00:30:45,211 --> 00:30:47,813
That one! That one!
That one!

382
00:30:51,217 --> 00:30:52,218
Careful.

383
00:30:52,751 --> 00:30:54,120
Sorry.

384
00:30:58,690 --> 00:31:00,192
I'm sorry, Johnny.

385
00:31:00,259 --> 00:31:02,929
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Johnny.
I'm sorry.

386
00:31:02,995 --> 00:31:03,996
You okay.

387
00:31:11,904 --> 00:31:13,539
Hanna!

388
00:31:13,605 --> 00:31:14,573
Hanna!

389
00:31:15,407 --> 00:31:16,909
Hanna!

390
00:31:20,112 --> 00:31:22,081
What the hell is
going on out there?

391
00:31:22,148 --> 00:31:23,849
Yellow Jackets
still looking to

392
00:31:23,916 --> 00:31:25,651
get on track.
Marcum back to pass.

393
00:31:25,717 --> 00:31:27,253
Intercepted!

394
00:32:12,531 --> 00:32:15,467
Don't quit! Don't quit!
Don't quit!

395
00:32:18,470 --> 00:32:20,939
Go! Go!

396
00:32:45,897 --> 00:32:48,167
That was a good one.
I liked that one.

397
00:32:49,268 --> 00:32:51,503
Radio!

398
00:32:51,570 --> 00:32:54,840
Hi, everybody. Hi, everybody.
Hi, everybody.

399
00:33:03,249 --> 00:33:05,517
Quite a show you
put on tonight.

400
00:33:05,584 --> 00:33:07,519
Just wondering if
you were running

401
00:33:07,586 --> 00:33:09,755
a football program
or a social club.

402
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:34,513
Radio, I need to talk to your mama.
That okay?

403
00:33:35,847 --> 00:33:37,483
She right there.

404
00:33:42,388 --> 00:33:43,989
Hi, Mama.

405
00:33:44,056 --> 00:33:46,225
There's a sandwich
in there for you.

406
00:33:47,459 --> 00:33:48,594
I'll be in there directly.

407
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:49,795
Okay, Mama.

408
00:33:52,831 --> 00:33:54,166
Ma'am.

409
00:33:58,837 --> 00:34:01,307
I was wondering
if we might carry

410
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:03,942
your son tomorrow
on the team bus.

411
00:34:04,009 --> 00:34:06,212
Got us a football game.

412
00:34:06,278 --> 00:34:09,215
What your boys done to my son
was wrong...

413
00:34:09,281 --> 00:34:12,618
...but I don't expect you
to make up for it.

414
00:34:12,684 --> 00:34:15,221
The boys are
taking to him real good.

415
00:34:15,287 --> 00:34:18,023
They're still boys,
now, ain't they?

416
00:34:18,090 --> 00:34:19,991
I'll keep a good eye on him.

417
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:24,430
I guess it's
all right with me.

418
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:31,237
I don't mean to pry, ma'am...

419
00:34:32,104 --> 00:34:35,174
...but I was hoping...

420
00:34:35,241 --> 00:34:38,577
...I might be able to ask you
what exactly is wrong with him.

421
00:34:40,279 --> 00:34:43,115
Well, the doctors never could
give me a name for it.

422
00:34:43,182 --> 00:34:45,251
Say he the same
as everybody else,

423
00:34:45,317 --> 00:34:47,486
just a little
slower than most.

424
00:34:47,553 --> 00:34:50,856
I got a older boy, Walter.
He's fine and all.

425
00:34:52,591 --> 00:34:53,959
And their daddy?

426
00:35:00,366 --> 00:35:01,900
He died a while back.

427
00:35:03,869 --> 00:35:05,003
I'm sorry.

428
00:35:07,173 --> 00:35:08,974
You got your hands full.

429
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:11,143
Well,
they got me working 1 0 hours

430
00:35:11,210 --> 00:35:13,412
a day at the hospital.
Some days more.

431
00:35:13,479 --> 00:35:16,915
So I'm wondering where he's at
half the time...

432
00:35:16,982 --> 00:35:19,251
...and worrying all the time.

433
00:35:19,318 --> 00:35:22,854
Because I figure they only gonna need
one excuse to put him away.

434
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:30,629
James is a good boy, coach.
He got himself a good heart.

435
00:35:30,696 --> 00:35:34,333
Most folks just don't take the time
to see it, is all.

436
00:35:34,400 --> 00:35:35,601
James.

437
00:35:37,536 --> 00:35:39,605
James Robert Kennedy.

438
00:35:41,740 --> 00:35:43,108
Thank you, ma'am.

439
00:35:49,815 --> 00:35:52,618
No, he is not
getting on that bus.

440
00:35:52,684 --> 00:35:55,421
Harold, he is not a student.

441
00:35:55,487 --> 00:35:58,290
You don't even
know how old he is.

442
00:35:58,357 --> 00:36:01,327
Look, he has a handicap
we know nothing about.

443
00:36:01,393 --> 00:36:03,962
What if he has some kind
of a seizure?

444
00:36:04,029 --> 00:36:06,432
He's not the one who's
gonna have the seizure.

445
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:08,700
This has nothing to do
with any of that.

446
00:36:08,767 --> 00:36:11,102
If you're saying
I'm overly concerned...

447
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:12,971
...about my
students being with

448
00:36:13,038 --> 00:36:14,906
a severely
handicapped black man...

449
00:36:14,973 --> 00:36:16,808
...I assure you that I am.

450
00:36:16,875 --> 00:36:20,111
But my concern is not necessarily
for my students.

451
00:36:22,448 --> 00:36:25,217
I'm not so sure we're trying to help
somebody here...

452
00:36:25,284 --> 00:36:27,052
...or whether
he's being used as

453
00:36:27,118 --> 00:36:29,721
nothing more than
a glorified mascot.

454
00:36:29,788 --> 00:36:32,791
You know me a hell of a lot
better than that.

455
00:36:39,498 --> 00:36:42,033
Put your game face on.

456
00:36:42,100 --> 00:36:46,137
Wipe your smile off your faces.
Start thinking about football.

457
00:36:47,239 --> 00:36:48,640
Coach Jones. It raining hard.

458
00:36:48,707 --> 00:36:50,208
Radio. Radio.

459
00:36:50,276 --> 00:36:52,311
It sure is.
Gonna be wet out there.

460
00:36:52,378 --> 00:36:55,781
Listen, we're not gonna be able
to take you on the bus today.

461
00:36:57,516 --> 00:37:02,053
Some folks, they don't think
it's a good idea.

462
00:37:02,120 --> 00:37:03,822
They just don't
understand yet,

463
00:37:03,889 --> 00:37:06,057
but they'll catch on.
Believe me.

464
00:37:06,124 --> 00:37:07,493
I'm sorry.

465
00:37:08,394 --> 00:37:09,895
I'm really sorry.

466
00:37:12,364 --> 00:37:14,533
I'll see you tomorrow. Okay?

467
00:37:35,621 --> 00:37:37,323
And in local sports...

468
00:37:37,389 --> 00:37:39,124
...Hanna's
Yellow Jackets travel

469
00:37:39,190 --> 00:37:40,959
to Wade
Hampton tonight.

470
00:37:41,026 --> 00:37:42,694
With a 4-4 record,
they need to win

471
00:37:42,761 --> 00:37:44,463
both their
remaining games...

472
00:37:44,530 --> 00:37:47,065
...to keep their
playoff hopes alive.

473
00:37:49,067 --> 00:37:51,503
Clock winding down now
in the fourth quarter.

474
00:37:51,570 --> 00:37:54,172
The Yellow Jackets have trailed
all night long...

475
00:37:54,239 --> 00:37:58,544
...but now within striking distance,
trailing 1 4 to 1 3.

476
00:38:03,315 --> 00:38:06,418
Danny Marcum barks
out the signals.

477
00:38:06,485 --> 00:38:08,654
He's back to pass.

478
00:38:08,720 --> 00:38:10,422
Incomplete.

479
00:38:18,830 --> 00:38:22,468
Second down now.
Still time to mount one last drive.

480
00:38:22,534 --> 00:38:25,070
And there's the draw play.
Playing up the middle.

481
00:38:25,136 --> 00:38:28,507
To 5, 1 0.
First down, Jackets.

482
00:38:31,677 --> 00:38:34,813
Jackets will go
for a field goal to win it.

483
00:38:36,515 --> 00:38:38,750
Less than
a minute to play.

484
00:38:46,992 --> 00:38:49,260
Kick.
Here's the snap.
The kick.

485
00:38:49,761 --> 00:38:51,463
No good!

486
00:38:53,298 --> 00:38:56,468
The Jackets'
last-ditch efforts fall short.

487
00:38:56,535 --> 00:39:01,106
Final score: Wade Hampton, 1 4,
Hanna, 1 3.

488
00:39:13,318 --> 00:39:15,654
Here, here. Use a spoon.

489
00:39:15,721 --> 00:39:17,022
There you go.

490
00:39:17,088 --> 00:39:18,724
I'll get some of
these out of your way.

491
00:39:18,790 --> 00:39:20,559
All right.

492
00:39:20,626 --> 00:39:21,893
Thank you, Grace.

493
00:39:21,960 --> 00:39:23,294
Which cobbler you got today?

494
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:25,030
I got so--

495
00:39:25,096 --> 00:39:26,532
I'm not done.

496
00:39:26,598 --> 00:39:28,800
Don't talk with
your mouth full, now.

497
00:39:30,035 --> 00:39:31,670
Peach and blackberry.

498
00:39:31,737 --> 00:39:33,472
Peach and blackberry.

499
00:39:33,539 --> 00:39:35,541
What's it gonna be, Radio?

500
00:39:35,607 --> 00:39:36,575
Both.

501
00:39:38,076 --> 00:39:41,413
Give the man both.
I'd like some more coffee too, please.

502
00:39:41,480 --> 00:39:42,948
Yeah, I take both.

503
00:39:44,483 --> 00:39:45,484
Radio, look at me.

504
00:39:45,551 --> 00:39:46,718
I want my pie.

505
00:39:46,785 --> 00:39:49,821
You got mustard on your cheek.
Get it for you.

506
00:39:49,888 --> 00:39:51,389
There you go.

507
00:39:56,728 --> 00:39:58,830
Football season's
just about over.

508
00:39:59,831 --> 00:40:00,866
You know that, don't you?

509
00:40:00,932 --> 00:40:02,067
One more game.

510
00:40:02,133 --> 00:40:04,135
Yep. One more game.

511
00:40:04,202 --> 00:40:06,037
You gonna be okay with that?

512
00:40:10,141 --> 00:40:12,210
Where my pie?

513
00:40:12,277 --> 00:40:14,446
Don't worry, they're coming.

514
00:40:14,513 --> 00:40:16,815
She'll bring you your pie.
Don't worry.

515
00:40:16,882 --> 00:40:18,183
I like both.

516
00:40:18,249 --> 00:40:19,785
She's got your order.

517
00:40:21,787 --> 00:40:25,524
Football. I like football.

518
00:40:25,591 --> 00:40:27,793
Some of us felt
pretty bad about

519
00:40:27,859 --> 00:40:29,995
leaving you off
that bus last night.

520
00:40:32,230 --> 00:40:34,766
We're gonna find a way
to make it up to you.

521
00:40:36,568 --> 00:40:38,470
How you gonna do that, coach?

522
00:40:42,774 --> 00:40:47,479
Your Hanna
Yellow Jackets!

523
00:40:50,148 --> 00:40:52,518
Jackets!

524
00:40:55,253 --> 00:40:56,555
All right!

525
00:41:03,061 --> 00:41:04,930
We're having fun.
This is a good one.

526
00:41:04,996 --> 00:41:06,932
This is a good one.

527
00:41:06,998 --> 00:41:08,734
Nothing like
archrival Westside

528
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:10,602
to get Jackets
fans stirred up.

529
00:41:10,669 --> 00:41:13,639
Winning this one would even Hanna's
record at 5 and 5...

530
00:41:13,705 --> 00:41:16,174
...and though a far cry
from early season hopes...

531
00:41:16,241 --> 00:41:19,645
...salvage a measure of pride
for the home squad.

532
00:41:21,179 --> 00:41:24,415
Here we go. Here we go.

533
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:27,252
All right, 4 right,
2 4 flank and reverse.

534
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:28,754
Third and 6 on the 40.

535
00:41:28,820 --> 00:41:30,355
That was a good one, coach.

536
00:41:30,421 --> 00:41:31,489
We'll see.

537
00:41:31,557 --> 00:41:32,691
Ready!

538
00:41:32,758 --> 00:41:34,492
That was a reverse! Reverse!

539
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:35,927
Reverse!

540
00:41:35,994 --> 00:41:37,128
Come back here.

541
00:41:37,195 --> 00:41:38,964
What--?
He's telling the play!

542
00:41:39,030 --> 00:41:40,732
Westside defense
calling an audible,

543
00:41:40,799 --> 00:41:42,568
brings in both
linebackers.

544
00:41:42,634 --> 00:41:44,402
Reverse!
Danny, check it off.

545
00:41:44,469 --> 00:41:47,806
Jones signaling for time, but Marcum
doesn't hear him.

546
00:41:47,873 --> 00:41:49,440
Marcum rolls right,
pitches it

547
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:51,176
to Hill on
a flank and reverse.

548
00:41:51,242 --> 00:41:55,681
He is crushed in the backfield
and fumbles the ball.

549
00:41:55,747 --> 00:41:57,215
It's recovered
by Westside!

550
00:41:57,282 --> 00:41:58,684
Daggum it!

551
00:41:59,450 --> 00:42:00,518
Come on.

552
00:42:02,187 --> 00:42:05,123
No wonder! They knew the play.
They knew the play!

553
00:42:05,190 --> 00:42:07,392
Defense, get out there.

554
00:42:07,458 --> 00:42:09,628
Radio, listen to me.
You can't let the

555
00:42:09,695 --> 00:42:12,263
other team know
what we're gonna do.

556
00:42:12,330 --> 00:42:13,565
How they know that, coach?

557
00:42:13,632 --> 00:42:14,966
Tommy, get out there!

558
00:42:15,033 --> 00:42:16,534
Good God.

559
00:42:16,602 --> 00:42:18,469
Set! Hike!

560
00:42:18,536 --> 00:42:20,939
Snead back to
pass for Westside.

561
00:42:22,307 --> 00:42:23,975
It's broken up,
but a flag is thrown

562
00:42:24,042 --> 00:42:25,777
on
the Jackets' cornerback.

563
00:42:25,844 --> 00:42:27,245
No!

564
00:42:27,312 --> 00:42:28,513
Got him in the back, coach.

565
00:42:28,580 --> 00:42:29,848
Are you kidding?!

566
00:42:29,915 --> 00:42:31,650
You blew that
call and you know it.

567
00:42:31,717 --> 00:42:33,518
You need to move back.

568
00:42:33,585 --> 00:42:35,520
Don't do it. Don't do it.

569
00:42:35,587 --> 00:42:37,623
That was a chickenshit call.

570
00:42:37,689 --> 00:42:39,557
Oh, come on!
Fifteen more!

571
00:42:39,625 --> 00:42:41,359
Another
penalty on Jones.

572
00:42:41,426 --> 00:42:43,428
Chickenshit! Chickenshit!

573
00:42:43,494 --> 00:42:45,597
Fifteen more.
Go to the white line.

574
00:42:45,664 --> 00:42:47,432
Chickenshit! Chickenshit!

575
00:42:47,498 --> 00:42:49,067
Radio! Get him out
of there, Honeycutt!

576
00:42:49,134 --> 00:42:50,836
Get him back.

577
00:42:50,902 --> 00:42:52,537
Unsportsmanlike conduct!

578
00:42:52,604 --> 00:42:55,373
Just called a third penalty
on the Jackets' bench.

579
00:42:55,440 --> 00:42:57,575
It looks like a train wreck
down there.

580
00:42:57,643 --> 00:43:00,145
Honeycutt,
get him off the field.

581
00:43:00,211 --> 00:43:03,581
How many flags you got?!
You got any more flags?!

582
00:43:03,649 --> 00:43:05,050
Get him back!

583
00:43:05,116 --> 00:43:06,618
A total of 45
yards now on the play.

584
00:43:06,685 --> 00:43:07,686
There goes my evening.

585
00:43:07,753 --> 00:43:08,787
Come on, Radio.

586
00:43:08,854 --> 00:43:11,022
Let's go, buddy. Here we go.

587
00:43:17,929 --> 00:43:19,597
Any chance I can get the ball?

588
00:43:19,665 --> 00:43:22,600
Nobody speaks in here
unless Coach Jones says he does.

589
00:43:22,668 --> 00:43:24,135
Sit down, Clay.

590
00:43:29,207 --> 00:43:30,676
There your ball.

591
00:43:35,714 --> 00:43:38,383
Now that we got
that taken care of...

592
00:43:43,922 --> 00:43:46,758
Jackets trying to hold Westside
in the fourth quarter.

593
00:43:46,825 --> 00:43:48,626
They've stiffened
here in the second

594
00:43:48,694 --> 00:43:51,196
half and still
trail by only 4.

595
00:43:51,262 --> 00:43:53,464
Here comes
the Jackets' blitz.

596
00:43:55,300 --> 00:43:56,467
He got him! He got him!

597
00:43:56,534 --> 00:43:57,769
He got him!

598
00:43:57,836 --> 00:43:58,937
Go!

599
00:43:59,004 --> 00:44:00,772
The ball will go
back to the Jackets

600
00:44:00,839 --> 00:44:03,008
with time for
one last drive.

601
00:44:07,178 --> 00:44:08,179
Hut!

602
00:44:09,715 --> 00:44:12,350
Marcum keeps it.
Pitches to Smalls.

603
00:44:12,417 --> 00:44:17,155
Bounces off one tackler
and breaks free. Touchdown, Jackets!

604
00:44:17,222 --> 00:44:19,124
Good job. Come here.

605
00:44:19,190 --> 00:44:21,626
Flanker right, split left.
Twenty-four

606
00:44:21,693 --> 00:44:24,095
Z post.
Get on your horse, now.

607
00:44:26,597 --> 00:44:28,633
Hey, Honeycutt...

608
00:44:28,700 --> 00:44:30,836
...I got a good
feeling about this one.

609
00:44:30,902 --> 00:44:32,971
Good feeling. Good feeling.

610
00:44:35,373 --> 00:44:37,108
Set! Hut!

611
00:44:37,175 --> 00:44:40,478
Marcum fakes
the handoff
and drops back to pass.

612
00:44:40,545 --> 00:44:42,047
Looking long.

613
00:44:42,748 --> 00:44:44,349
Mitchell's open.

614
00:44:46,351 --> 00:44:49,955
Touchdown,
Yellow Jackets!

615
00:44:50,021 --> 00:44:51,857
Oh! That was a good one!

616
00:44:51,923 --> 00:44:53,892
Good one! What'd I tell you?

617
00:44:53,959 --> 00:44:56,027
With less than
a minute to play, Hanna

618
00:44:56,094 --> 00:44:58,196
has overtaken
rival Westside...

619
00:44:58,263 --> 00:45:01,733
...with a stunning
37-yard touchdown.

620
00:45:07,338 --> 00:45:11,209
That's the way the game's
supposed to be played. Good job.

621
00:45:17,648 --> 00:45:19,851
Settle down, now. Listen up.

622
00:45:19,918 --> 00:45:23,688
That was a great
team effort out there
tonight. Great comeback.

623
00:45:23,755 --> 00:45:26,925
Y'all played your hearts out.
I'm proud of you. Good job.

624
00:45:28,326 --> 00:45:30,061
Honeycutt.

625
00:45:30,128 --> 00:45:33,865
For standing behind us all season long,
especially tonight...

626
00:45:33,932 --> 00:45:36,234
...the game ball...

627
00:45:36,301 --> 00:45:37,769
...goes to Radio.

628
00:45:52,784 --> 00:45:53,952
Can you sign this?

629
00:45:54,019 --> 00:45:55,120
Yeah, sure.

630
00:45:57,789 --> 00:45:58,790
There you go.

631
00:45:58,857 --> 00:46:00,091
Thanks.

632
00:46:00,158 --> 00:46:01,292
Hey. How are you?

633
00:46:01,359 --> 00:46:02,760
Much better now.

634
00:46:02,828 --> 00:46:06,197
Yeah? You want me to bring
this home tonight?

635
00:46:06,264 --> 00:46:07,765
You only got one of them?

636
00:46:07,833 --> 00:46:09,334
I had a lot to
choose from, didn't I?

637
00:46:09,400 --> 00:46:11,036
No kidding, huh?

638
00:46:11,102 --> 00:46:12,838
You going over to the shop?

639
00:46:12,904 --> 00:46:14,705
I suspect so.
Shouldn't be too painful.

640
00:46:14,772 --> 00:46:16,975
Well,
don't forget to bring some of

641
00:46:17,042 --> 00:46:19,377
that
unsportsmanlike conduct home.

642
00:46:19,444 --> 00:46:21,079
All right.

643
00:46:24,749 --> 00:46:26,651
Harold.
Evening, fellas.

644
00:46:26,717 --> 00:46:28,619
Irv. Clive.

645
00:46:28,686 --> 00:46:30,555
Nice win tonight, coach.

646
00:46:34,225 --> 00:46:36,261
I'll make us a fresh batch.

647
00:46:36,327 --> 00:46:38,329
Well, this will be fine, Del.

648
00:46:41,900 --> 00:46:47,138
Well, l know a .500 season
isn't what we all had in mind...

649
00:46:47,205 --> 00:46:51,009
...but I did see some things tonight
I think we can build on.

650
00:46:51,076 --> 00:46:53,979
The boys made good adjustments
at halftime...

651
00:46:54,045 --> 00:46:56,848
...and Danny
Marcum finally got
the offense moving.

652
00:46:56,915 --> 00:46:57,916
He sure did.

653
00:46:57,983 --> 00:46:59,250
He sure did, coach.

654
00:46:59,317 --> 00:47:01,652
I'm real proud
of all the boys.

655
00:47:03,321 --> 00:47:07,692
Always good to beat Westside,
and it's nice to win the last one.

656
00:47:07,758 --> 00:47:11,396
Wasn't long ago we were winning
most every one.

657
00:47:11,462 --> 00:47:13,764
There something you need
to say, Frank?

658
00:47:15,867 --> 00:47:17,635
Well...

659
00:47:17,702 --> 00:47:21,940
...I think we got too good a team
to be losing half our games.

660
00:47:27,979 --> 00:47:29,214
Anybody else?

661
00:47:32,850 --> 00:47:34,886
It's all right,
you can speak up.

662
00:47:37,688 --> 00:47:41,292
Well, if nobody else is gonna
say anything, I sure as hell will.

663
00:47:43,461 --> 00:47:46,297
You got yourself a distraction
needs dealing with.

664
00:47:46,898 --> 00:47:48,499
A distraction?

665
00:47:51,169 --> 00:47:53,604
That what you think Radio is?

666
00:47:53,671 --> 00:47:55,573
Well, you're damn right I do.

667
00:47:55,640 --> 00:47:57,142
Come on, now, Frank.

668
00:48:02,180 --> 00:48:06,184
You know, I think I'm gonna
do us all a big favor...

669
00:48:06,251 --> 00:48:08,954
...and let you
all finish this one on your own.

670
00:48:16,962 --> 00:48:18,696
Coffee's been better, Del.

671
00:48:19,397 --> 00:48:20,932
Sorry, coach.

672
00:48:33,478 --> 00:48:35,646
Well, now you show up.

673
00:48:35,713 --> 00:48:37,848
You chickenshit.

674
00:48:37,915 --> 00:48:40,251
I figured I'd
just be in the way.

675
00:48:41,619 --> 00:48:42,988
How'd it go?

676
00:48:46,091 --> 00:48:49,060
That good, huh?

677
00:48:49,127 --> 00:48:52,830
I'm afraid we've got
a disgruntled booster on our hands.

678
00:48:53,664 --> 00:48:55,766
Banker Frank?

679
00:48:55,833 --> 00:49:01,172
Yeah, he says we got a problem
with Radio being on the sidelines.

680
00:49:06,677 --> 00:49:08,446
What do you think?

681
00:49:13,018 --> 00:49:14,952
I think that one's up to you.

682
00:49:20,625 --> 00:49:23,628
How's
the basketball team looking?

683
00:49:23,694 --> 00:49:27,398
Just fine long as Johnny
stays healthy. Why?

684
00:49:27,465 --> 00:49:30,835
Oh, I just thought Radio
might need something to do.

685
00:49:35,906 --> 00:49:37,575
I reckon we
could use some help.

686
00:49:37,642 --> 00:49:39,377
Good.

687
00:49:39,444 --> 00:49:40,945
I'll see you Monday.

688
00:49:49,020 --> 00:49:52,457
Hey, what you got now, boy?

689
00:49:52,523 --> 00:49:54,492
Football. Football.

690
00:49:54,559 --> 00:49:57,728
A football? Coach Jones
gave you that?

691
00:49:57,795 --> 00:49:59,197
Yeah.

692
00:50:01,332 --> 00:50:03,401
Wait a minute, now.

693
00:50:04,502 --> 00:50:06,137
What's the matter?

694
00:50:09,874 --> 00:50:11,442
We all done.

695
00:50:11,509 --> 00:50:13,178
Oh, now.

696
00:50:13,244 --> 00:50:17,615
We all knew the season
was gonna end sometime. Yeah?

697
00:50:19,584 --> 00:50:21,086
But look what you got.

698
00:50:21,152 --> 00:50:23,588
A football...

699
00:50:23,654 --> 00:50:26,324
...and a sweatshirt.

700
00:50:26,391 --> 00:50:28,959
And lookie here.
Look at all of this.

701
00:50:29,827 --> 00:50:31,529
Look at that.

702
00:50:31,596 --> 00:50:32,830
That Radio.

703
00:50:32,897 --> 00:50:34,999
Yeah.

704
00:50:35,066 --> 00:50:38,569
See,
now, next fall gonna be here before you know it.

705
00:50:38,636 --> 00:50:40,037
Promise.

706
00:50:41,506 --> 00:50:43,608
Now, give Mama a hug.

707
00:50:45,676 --> 00:50:47,512
Boy, what's that?

708
00:50:48,579 --> 00:50:50,448
I want me a hug.

709
00:50:54,485 --> 00:50:57,054
I'm always here for you, baby.

710
00:50:59,790 --> 00:51:01,726
President-elect
Carter met President

711
00:51:01,792 --> 00:51:03,794
Ford today at
the White House.

712
00:51:03,861 --> 00:51:06,931
Also meeting
with CIA boss George Bush.

713
00:51:06,997 --> 00:51:08,866
The New York Post
has been sold to

714
00:51:08,933 --> 00:51:10,868
Australian
publisher Rupert Murdoch.

715
00:51:10,935 --> 00:51:12,737
Morning.
Morning, girls.

716
00:51:12,803 --> 00:51:15,573
Free agent
Reggie Jackson signed a five-year deal...

717
00:51:15,640 --> 00:51:18,276
...to play with
the New York Yankees.

718
00:51:35,360 --> 00:51:37,195
Hi.
Hi, Nicole.

719
00:51:37,262 --> 00:51:38,596
Coach Jones.

720
00:51:38,663 --> 00:51:40,731
Good morning.
Good morning, Lou.

721
00:51:40,798 --> 00:51:42,533
What brings you around here?

722
00:51:42,600 --> 00:51:44,669
Seeing as you never
drop by my office,

723
00:51:44,735 --> 00:51:46,904
I thought I'd
pop up for a visit.

724
00:51:46,971 --> 00:51:48,639
And how is everything?

725
00:51:48,706 --> 00:51:50,475
Everything's fine. Why?

726
00:51:50,541 --> 00:51:52,710
A little bird says Mr.
Kennedy's spent

727
00:51:52,777 --> 00:51:55,012
time with you
inside the building.

728
00:51:55,079 --> 00:51:57,248
Yeah, that's correct.

729
00:51:57,315 --> 00:51:59,217
Do you see that
as a problem?

730
00:51:59,284 --> 00:52:02,019
Disrupting a football game
is one thing.

731
00:52:02,086 --> 00:52:04,822
Disrupting a classroom
is a different matter.

732
00:52:07,192 --> 00:52:10,795
I want him with you all the time.
Okay?

733
00:52:10,861 --> 00:52:12,129
Yes, ma'am.

734
00:52:13,631 --> 00:52:16,967
--I-O.

735
00:52:17,034 --> 00:52:19,136
''Radio.''

736
00:52:19,204 --> 00:52:21,772
And that's how you spell it.

737
00:52:21,839 --> 00:52:23,574
Here, you want to try it?

738
00:52:24,942 --> 00:52:26,644
You want to do it?

739
00:52:26,711 --> 00:52:31,749
Look. It's easy. You just take
the chalk and it writes right on there.

740
00:52:31,816 --> 00:52:34,819
All right, well, we don't
have to do it right now.

741
00:52:34,885 --> 00:52:36,354
Radio.

742
00:52:41,826 --> 00:52:45,363
Blueberry and pumpkin today.
Pie, not cobbler.

743
00:52:46,797 --> 00:52:48,065
Both.

744
00:52:54,939 --> 00:52:58,075
Coach Jones,
you're needed in the office.

745
00:52:58,142 --> 00:53:01,246
All right, everybody,
just keep working.

746
00:53:01,312 --> 00:53:04,949
Radio, keep everybody under control
while l'm gone, now.

747
00:53:05,015 --> 00:53:06,751
Keep an eye on everything.

748
00:53:11,622 --> 00:53:13,491
No talking. No talking.

749
00:53:13,558 --> 00:53:15,526
No talking. No--

750
00:53:18,062 --> 00:53:20,798
Well, now, how long
would you say Mr. Kennedy...

751
00:53:20,865 --> 00:53:23,601
...has been in
an actual classroom setting?

752
00:53:23,668 --> 00:53:26,704
Well,
let's see, about a month.

753
00:53:28,439 --> 00:53:30,174
And the thinking behind that?

754
00:53:30,241 --> 00:53:33,344
He was doing fine with the team.
I didn't see any harm in it.

755
00:53:40,451 --> 00:53:42,587
Mr. Tucker, I know you got a job
to do...

756
00:53:42,653 --> 00:53:44,589
...but is me
having Radio in the

757
00:53:44,655 --> 00:53:47,625
classroom really
worth all this trouble?

758
00:53:47,692 --> 00:53:50,728
That's what the school board
would like to find out.

759
00:53:50,795 --> 00:53:54,565
This is a young man who's been
spending his entire lifetime...

760
00:53:54,632 --> 00:53:57,702
...wandering around all by himself
out on the streets.

761
00:53:57,768 --> 00:54:01,539
Which is quite different than being
inside a public school. Right?

762
00:54:01,606 --> 00:54:04,542
Yeah, well, that's the point,
isn't it?

763
00:54:04,609 --> 00:54:06,143
Mr. Tucker...

764
00:54:06,210 --> 00:54:09,380
...I am well aware of the liability risk
we are running here.

765
00:54:09,447 --> 00:54:11,416
Harold will be first
to tell you, my list

766
00:54:11,482 --> 00:54:13,551
of reservations is
longer than most.

767
00:54:13,618 --> 00:54:16,487
I'm sure that's the case.

768
00:54:16,554 --> 00:54:20,157
But the fact of the matter is,
none of us has
any experience...

769
00:54:20,224 --> 00:54:22,327
...with having
a severely retarded man

770
00:54:22,393 --> 00:54:24,662
wandering the halls
with our students.

771
00:54:25,496 --> 00:54:27,031
The risk is enormous.

772
00:54:27,097 --> 00:54:28,132
Please keep that in mind.

773
00:54:28,198 --> 00:54:29,199
I will.

774
00:54:31,802 --> 00:54:32,970
Ms. Daniels.

775
00:54:34,204 --> 00:54:35,840
Mr. Jones.

776
00:54:35,906 --> 00:54:37,508
Thank you, Mr. Tucker.

777
00:54:41,612 --> 00:54:45,916
Well, this is a hell of a position
you've put me in.

778
00:54:45,983 --> 00:54:50,321
Yeah, I suppose it is, Lou.
But Radio's not gonna do anything.

779
00:54:50,955 --> 00:54:52,122
Harold.

780
00:54:53,391 --> 00:54:55,760
Why on earth are
you doing this?

781
00:54:59,397 --> 00:55:01,065
Same reason you are.

782
00:55:04,502 --> 00:55:05,903
Defense.

783
00:55:05,970 --> 00:55:07,338
Defense. Come on.

784
00:55:10,040 --> 00:55:12,142
I'm good. I'm good.
How you doing?

