01:09:49,353 --> 01:09:50,520
Bring it up!

1046
01:09:51,588 --> 01:09:54,291
Take a pick!

1047
01:09:54,358 --> 01:09:57,661
Clay working off the pick.
Drives right side.

1048
01:09:59,195 --> 01:10:00,530
No basket! No!

1049
01:10:00,597 --> 01:10:02,031
Offensive foul,
Johnny Clay.

1050
01:10:02,098 --> 01:10:03,900
15 out of control.

1051
01:10:03,967 --> 01:10:05,835
You're killing me.
Time-out! Time-out!

1052
01:10:05,902 --> 01:10:08,538
Ref!
Did you think about that?!

1053
01:10:08,605 --> 01:10:10,006
Morning.

1054
01:10:10,073 --> 01:10:11,741
Morning, Radio.
Morning.

1055
01:10:11,808 --> 01:10:13,042
Morning.

1056
01:10:13,109 --> 01:10:14,278
Morning.

1057
01:10:15,479 --> 01:10:18,548
Radio. Where's my hug?

1058
01:10:20,216 --> 01:10:22,118
There it is.

1059
01:10:22,185 --> 01:10:23,553
Who'd you catch
running in the hall?

1060
01:10:23,620 --> 01:10:25,021
Billy Samson.

1061
01:10:25,088 --> 01:10:29,025
Swear, you have turned out
to be quite the hall monitor.

1062
01:10:31,194 --> 01:10:32,662
Morning, Hanna.

1063
01:10:32,729 --> 01:10:36,900
You know who this is?
This is Radio.

1064
01:10:36,966 --> 01:10:40,203
Today our menu is
Salisbury steak.

1065
01:10:40,270 --> 01:10:41,471
French fries.

1066
01:10:41,538 --> 01:10:42,839
French fri-- Oh, I like them.

1067
01:10:42,906 --> 01:10:44,274
Black-eyed peas.

1068
01:10:44,341 --> 01:10:45,575
Black-eye-- We
got black-eyed peas?

1069
01:10:45,642 --> 01:10:46,910
We sure do.

1070
01:10:46,976 --> 01:10:48,177
We got black-eyed peas.

1071
01:10:48,244 --> 01:10:49,379
Brownies.

1072
01:10:49,446 --> 01:10:50,647
We got brownies.

1073
01:10:50,714 --> 01:10:52,282
We got hot rolls.
Hot rolls.

1074
01:10:52,349 --> 01:10:53,483
And pear halves.

1075
01:10:53,550 --> 01:10:54,751
And what?

1076
01:10:54,818 --> 01:10:56,853
We have pear halves.
Pear halves.

1077
01:11:12,369 --> 01:11:14,304
Yeah.
Hey, we'll see you later.

1078
01:11:17,140 --> 01:11:18,542
Hey, yo.

1079
01:11:19,142 --> 01:11:20,377
Radio.

1080
01:11:20,444 --> 01:11:21,511
Hey, how you doing?

1081
01:11:21,578 --> 01:11:22,746
What's going on?

1082
01:11:22,812 --> 01:11:24,748
Hey,
where's Honeycutt at, man?

1083
01:11:24,814 --> 01:11:26,816
He gone.
Coach Honeycutt, he around?

1084
01:11:26,883 --> 01:11:28,918
Yeah, he gone.
He's gone. All right.

1085
01:11:28,985 --> 01:11:31,187
Coach Dalrymple's
got a couple things

1086
01:11:31,254 --> 01:11:33,423
next door she
wants you to come get.

1087
01:11:33,957 --> 01:11:35,425
Mrs. Dalrymple.

1088
01:11:35,492 --> 01:11:38,695
Don't worry, it's just her.
She's alone. Girls are gone.

1089
01:11:39,295 --> 01:11:41,331
I can't do that.

1090
01:11:41,398 --> 01:11:45,034
All right, man. All right,
but she's gonna be real disappointed.

1091
01:11:45,101 --> 01:11:47,471
You don't want to
let her down, do you?

1092
01:11:49,406 --> 01:11:51,375
See you.
Okay, Radio.

1093
01:12:21,905 --> 01:12:23,306
Mrs. Dalrymple?

1094
01:12:27,777 --> 01:12:29,312
Mrs. Dalrymple?

1095
01:12:32,549 --> 01:12:33,950
Radio!

1096
01:12:34,017 --> 01:12:35,785
You can't be in here.

1097
01:12:43,693 --> 01:12:45,495
Bad Radio. Bad Radio.

1098
01:12:46,796 --> 01:12:48,998
Coach Jones. Coach Jones.

1099
01:12:49,065 --> 01:12:52,536
Coach Jones. No, Radio.
No, Radio. No.

1100
01:12:55,071 --> 01:12:57,240
It'd be one
thing if you had done

1101
01:12:57,306 --> 01:12:59,609
something like this
before on your own.

1102
01:13:03,146 --> 01:13:05,849
Radio, listen to me.

1103
01:13:05,915 --> 01:13:07,884
It's important
that you tell me why

1104
01:13:07,951 --> 01:13:10,053
you went in
the girls' locker room.

1105
01:13:10,119 --> 01:13:11,588
Mrs. Dalrymple needed me.

1106
01:13:11,655 --> 01:13:13,056
What for?

1107
01:13:16,225 --> 01:13:17,761
She wanted me
to pick up stuff.

1108
01:13:17,827 --> 01:13:19,295
Did she ask you?

1109
01:13:19,863 --> 01:13:21,598
Did she ask you?

1110
01:13:22,732 --> 01:13:23,833
No.

1111
01:13:23,900 --> 01:13:24,934
Who did?

1112
01:13:25,935 --> 01:13:28,438
No.

1113
01:13:28,505 --> 01:13:31,475
Radio, who asked you to go
in the girls' locker room?

1114
01:13:33,477 --> 01:13:34,711
Who asked you?

1115
01:13:37,714 --> 01:13:39,015
No.

1116
01:13:44,721 --> 01:13:47,190
I don't know what I'm supposed
to do here.

1117
01:13:47,256 --> 01:13:48,892
Be mad at Radio.

1118
01:13:49,559 --> 01:13:51,327
Be mad at Radio.

1119
01:14:01,270 --> 01:14:03,306
You're willing to do that?

1120
01:14:03,372 --> 01:14:05,575
Take the blame
for someone else?

1121
01:14:12,849 --> 01:14:16,119
You're a better man than me.
I'll say that for you.

1122
01:14:31,535 --> 01:14:32,836
Hey, Johnny, what's up?

1123
01:14:32,902 --> 01:14:35,338
I got a letter last
week from Clemson.

1124
01:14:35,404 --> 01:14:38,842
They're looking at me for a full ride
after next year.

1125
01:14:38,908 --> 01:14:40,109
That's great.

1126
01:14:40,176 --> 01:14:41,511
Excuse me, gentlemen.

1127
01:14:41,578 --> 01:14:44,280
Excuse me. I need to speak
with Mr. Clay.

1128
01:14:44,347 --> 01:14:45,348
See you, Johnny.

1129
01:14:45,414 --> 01:14:46,583
What's up, coach?

1130
01:14:46,650 --> 01:14:48,351
It's one of those
days I wish I wasn't

1131
01:14:48,417 --> 01:14:50,520
a teacher so I
could lay into you.

1132
01:14:50,587 --> 01:14:52,622
What you talking about?

1133
01:14:53,590 --> 01:14:55,024
What's gotten into you?

1134
01:14:55,091 --> 01:14:56,760
I thought you'd
learned something

1135
01:14:56,826 --> 01:14:58,562
the past few months.
I was wrong.

1136
01:14:58,628 --> 01:15:00,396
What are you talking about?

1137
01:15:00,463 --> 01:15:02,498
Don't speak
unless I tell you to.

1138
01:15:05,234 --> 01:15:07,470
You might think
you're clear because

1139
01:15:07,537 --> 01:15:09,906
Honeycutt was gone,
but this is my call.

1140
01:15:11,775 --> 01:15:14,878
There's no way you're suiting up
tomorrow night.

1141
01:15:16,179 --> 01:15:17,380
Right.

1142
01:15:18,147 --> 01:15:20,049
What did you say?

1143
01:15:20,116 --> 01:15:22,118
Coach Jones. Mr. Clay.

1144
01:15:22,185 --> 01:15:23,620
What seems to be the problem?

1145
01:15:23,687 --> 01:15:25,622
You hear the problem.

1146
01:15:25,689 --> 01:15:29,492
Young man, students do not tell me
what I do and do not hear.

1147
01:15:30,326 --> 01:15:32,796
He said I can't play tomorrow.

1148
01:15:32,862 --> 01:15:34,798
Is that what
you're thinking, coach?

1149
01:15:34,864 --> 01:15:36,866
That's what I'm saying.

1150
01:15:36,933 --> 01:15:40,536
Well, then, seeing that Coach Jones
is the athletic director...

1151
01:15:40,604 --> 01:15:42,471
...I say you are not playing.

1152
01:15:42,538 --> 01:15:46,309
Ma'am, this is Westside.
If we win, we're in first place.

1153
01:15:46,375 --> 01:15:48,177
That's all
the more reason for you

1154
01:15:48,244 --> 01:15:50,113
to cheer on your teammates,
isn't it?

1155
01:15:50,179 --> 01:15:51,881
Anything else?

1156
01:15:54,984 --> 01:15:57,453
Yeah, tell your boy
that I said thanks.

1157
01:15:57,520 --> 01:16:00,223
Radio didn't
sell you out, son.

1158
01:16:00,289 --> 01:16:03,159
There are plenty of other people
willing to do that.

1159
01:16:10,566 --> 01:16:13,069
Yes, sir.

1160
01:16:13,136 --> 01:16:16,139
Well, I appreciate
your understanding.

1161
01:16:16,205 --> 01:16:18,675
We'll talk soon. Thank you.

1162
01:16:22,979 --> 01:16:25,314
That's the last of them.

1163
01:16:25,381 --> 01:16:26,883
You talk to Mary Helen yet?

1164
01:16:26,950 --> 01:16:29,953
Yeah, she's fine. She knows
it wasn't Radio's idea.

1165
01:16:30,019 --> 01:16:31,554
Oh, Harold.

1166
01:16:31,621 --> 01:16:34,858
Harold, you are too close
to this.

1167
01:16:34,924 --> 01:16:38,728
It's not that Johnny talked Radio into
doing it, it's that he did it.

1168
01:16:38,795 --> 01:16:41,430
What if it's something worse
next time?

1169
01:16:42,632 --> 01:16:44,033
He'll know.

1170
01:16:44,100 --> 01:16:46,402
Are you sure?

1171
01:16:46,469 --> 01:16:49,005
Hell, I'm already
under a microscope anyway.

1172
01:16:49,072 --> 01:16:52,141
I got a school to run,
a thousand kids i'm responsible for.

1173
01:16:52,208 --> 01:16:54,610
I need to know
where all this is going.

1174
01:16:54,678 --> 01:16:57,580
I don't know, Lou.

1175
01:16:57,647 --> 01:16:59,849
That may not be
good enough anymore.

1176
01:17:08,925 --> 01:17:10,994
I'm sorry.
I've been trying to call, and

1177
01:17:11,060 --> 01:17:13,229
I haven't gotten
ahold of either of them.

1178
01:17:13,296 --> 01:17:15,564
I tried several
different places.

1179
01:17:15,631 --> 01:17:18,134
Here he comes right now.
I'll tell him.

1180
01:17:20,136 --> 01:17:21,604
What's the matter?

1181
01:17:21,671 --> 01:17:23,272
It's Radio's mama, Daddy.

1182
01:17:23,339 --> 01:17:24,373
What happened?

1183
01:17:24,440 --> 01:17:25,574
She had a heart attack.

1184
01:17:25,641 --> 01:17:27,543
Oh, no. Is she all right?

1185
01:17:28,477 --> 01:17:30,313
No, she's gone.

1186
01:17:30,379 --> 01:17:34,851
I was trying to call you or Mom,
but I couldn't reach anybody.

1187
01:17:34,918 --> 01:17:39,655
And they're telling me
that he won't come out of his room.

1188
01:17:39,723 --> 01:17:41,424
I don't know
what to do, Daddy.

1189
01:17:41,490 --> 01:17:43,526
All right. Put your coat on.

1190
01:17:43,592 --> 01:17:46,696
He's just sitting
there in his room.

1191
01:17:46,763 --> 01:17:47,997
You got it?

1192
01:18:02,111 --> 01:18:03,246
Irv.

1193
01:18:03,312 --> 01:18:05,749
Coach, thanks for coming.

1194
01:18:05,815 --> 01:18:07,917
Walter will be
here in a few minutes.

1195
01:18:07,984 --> 01:18:09,685
How's Radio?

1196
01:18:09,753 --> 01:18:11,620
He's pretty upset.

1197
01:18:11,687 --> 01:18:13,890
Tore the place up
pretty good too.

1198
01:18:25,534 --> 01:18:26,936
Radio?

1199
01:19:11,781 --> 01:19:13,716
It's just me.
It's Coach Jones.

1200
01:19:24,060 --> 01:19:25,694
It's just coach.

1201
01:19:25,761 --> 01:19:27,230
Coach.

1202
01:19:28,998 --> 01:19:31,801
Coach. That's Radio.

1203
01:19:31,868 --> 01:19:32,936
Yeah.

1204
01:19:34,503 --> 01:19:35,872
That's you.

1205
01:19:35,939 --> 01:19:37,340
Radio right there.

1206
01:19:47,683 --> 01:19:52,321
There's Mama there. Mama said
we got good football this year.

1207
01:19:52,388 --> 01:19:53,522
Yes. Yeah.

1208
01:19:53,589 --> 01:19:55,959
That's what Mama said.
We got good--

1209
01:20:07,503 --> 01:20:09,205
Radio,
ain't nothing I can say is

1210
01:20:09,272 --> 01:20:11,207
gonna make you
feel any better.

1211
01:20:12,575 --> 01:20:14,177
Mama.

1212
01:20:14,243 --> 01:20:17,013
Your mama was a fine,
beautiful woman.

1213
01:20:17,080 --> 01:20:19,883
She loved you with all her heart,
didn't she?

1214
01:20:19,949 --> 01:20:22,351
Oh, boy, did she love you.

1215
01:20:24,520 --> 01:20:26,022
She still does.

1216
01:20:26,089 --> 01:20:27,523
She love the Radio.

1217
01:20:31,127 --> 01:20:34,330
She said she's always gonna
be there for Radio.

1218
01:20:39,002 --> 01:20:40,269
James...

1219
01:20:42,105 --> 01:20:43,572
...look at me.

1220
01:20:44,573 --> 01:20:46,542
Look at me.

1221
01:20:46,609 --> 01:20:50,146
She will always be there for you.
All right? She will.

1222
01:20:50,880 --> 01:20:52,916
You understand that?

1223
01:20:52,982 --> 01:20:56,719
Always be with you inside,
right in your heart. All right?

1224
01:21:07,430 --> 01:21:09,165
We're gonna be all right.

1225
01:21:11,067 --> 01:21:13,269
All right, boy.
Come here. Come here.

1226
01:21:15,038 --> 01:21:17,073
Where's my mama?

1227
01:21:29,385 --> 01:21:31,154
Hold on just a second.

1228
01:21:35,624 --> 01:21:37,526
I want to tell you something.

1229
01:21:40,196 --> 01:21:42,465
Something I never told anybody.

1230
01:21:45,034 --> 01:21:48,304
When I was about 12,
I had a paper route.

1231
01:21:50,473 --> 01:21:52,508
Crack of dawn every day.

1232
01:21:54,710 --> 01:21:57,913
Wasn't many houses
around here then...

1233
01:21:57,981 --> 01:22:00,883
...so   had to cover quite a lot
of territory...

1234
01:22:00,950 --> 01:22:06,289
...and I used to cut through
the woods on this little dirt road.

1235
01:22:06,355 --> 01:22:10,626
And one morning, I was riding
through there...

1236
01:22:10,693 --> 01:22:14,563
...and I heard this noise.

1237
01:22:14,630 --> 01:22:20,836
Sounded like a rabbit or something,
you know, caught in a trap.

1238
01:22:20,903 --> 01:22:22,871
And then I realized
it was coming from

1239
01:22:22,938 --> 01:22:25,108
one of the houses
set back in there.

1240
01:22:27,076 --> 01:22:28,944
I kind of walked over there...

1241
01:22:29,012 --> 01:22:32,815
...and didn't seem like anybody
was home, so I walked on up.

1242
01:22:32,881 --> 01:22:35,451
It had,
you know, chicken wire and

1243
01:22:35,518 --> 01:22:38,187
barbed wire around
the bottom of it.

1244
01:22:38,254 --> 01:22:40,789
I figure to keep the critters out,
you know?

1245
01:22:43,726 --> 01:22:46,062
And then all of the sudden,
I saw

1246
01:22:46,129 --> 01:22:48,431
these fingers
coming through the wire.

1247
01:22:50,066 --> 01:22:53,069
And I put my bike down...

1248
01:22:53,136 --> 01:22:56,405
...and got down
on my hands and knees...

1249
01:22:56,472 --> 01:23:02,211
...and I looked under there,
and there was this boy about my age.

1250
01:23:02,278 --> 01:23:06,582
I don't know what was wrong
with him. Something was.

1251
01:23:06,649 --> 01:23:09,018
They used to keep
him under there.

1252
01:23:09,085 --> 01:23:13,022
And I looked right at him.

1253
01:23:14,323 --> 01:23:16,425
He looked back at me.

1254
01:23:19,662 --> 01:23:22,731
We just sat there staring
at each other for a while.

1255
01:23:28,137 --> 01:23:31,374
I ran that route for two years,
Mary Helen.

1256
01:23:38,147 --> 01:23:40,283
And I never did a thing.

1257
01:23:52,795 --> 01:23:54,930
I just wanted
you to know that.

1258
01:23:57,133 --> 01:23:58,734
Thanks, Daddy.

1259
01:24:23,392 --> 01:24:24,727
How long before he comes back?

1260
01:24:24,793 --> 01:24:26,162
I'm hoping tomorrow.

1261
01:24:26,229 --> 01:24:28,631
His brother Walter's moved in
with him.

1262
01:24:28,697 --> 01:24:32,301
Honeycutt says he let loose
on that house pretty good.

1263
01:24:32,368 --> 01:24:35,204
Says he's not the only one
that knows about it either.

1264
01:24:35,271 --> 01:24:37,373
The man had just lost his
mother, Lou.

1265
01:24:37,440 --> 01:24:39,608
I didn't ask why he
took a swing at his

1266
01:24:39,675 --> 01:24:41,944
wall. I asked you
if you knew about it.

1267
01:24:42,010 --> 01:24:43,946
Why are you asking me that?

1268
01:24:48,417 --> 01:24:52,888
Our friend from
the board is back.
He wants to see you.

1269
01:24:52,955 --> 01:24:56,125
With his mama gone,
it's all different. Every bit of it.

1270
01:24:59,328 --> 01:25:00,463
Good luck.

1271
01:25:02,698 --> 01:25:07,670
In the last month,
how much time has Mr. Kennedy spent alone?

1272
01:25:08,871 --> 01:25:10,706
During the day at least.

1273
01:25:13,041 --> 01:25:15,010
Mr. Jones.

1274
01:25:15,077 --> 01:25:17,012
Past few weeks?
Everybody's been

1275
01:25:17,079 --> 01:25:20,183
keeping a pretty
steady eye on him.

1276
01:25:20,249 --> 01:25:22,551
So we talking an hour a day?
Or two?

1277
01:25:22,618 --> 01:25:25,621
An hour, maybe.
Well, it could be a half-hour.

1278
01:25:28,557 --> 01:25:30,493
Well,
as you may have guessed...

1279
01:25:30,559 --> 01:25:32,395
...the board has
received reports of

1280
01:25:32,461 --> 01:25:34,397
Mr. Kennedy's
inconsistent behavior.

1281
01:25:34,463 --> 01:25:36,465
What kind of reports?
From who?

1282
01:25:36,532 --> 01:25:39,468
Reports of resisting arrest...

1283
01:25:39,535 --> 01:25:42,671
...tearing up his home,
barging into the girls' locker room.

1284
01:25:42,738 --> 01:25:44,340
Oh, barging?

1285
01:25:44,407 --> 01:25:46,709
Who's been
feeding you this crap?

1286
01:25:46,775 --> 01:25:49,111
I'm not here to
argue with you.

1287
01:25:49,178 --> 01:25:51,113
I'm not arguing.
It's a simple question.

1288
01:25:51,180 --> 01:25:53,216
Who's been
feeding you this crap?

1289
01:25:54,617 --> 01:25:57,220
I ask because those
were all instances

1290
01:25:57,286 --> 01:25:59,955
in which he wasn't
being supervised.

1291
01:26:00,022 --> 01:26:01,023
Says who?

1292
01:26:03,459 --> 01:26:05,594
Says who?

1293
01:26:05,661 --> 01:26:08,331
Bottom line, with Ms.
Kennedy gone,

1294
01:26:08,397 --> 01:26:11,200
James faces some
rough times ahead.

1295
01:26:11,267 --> 01:26:12,868
To keep him in
a school setting--

1296
01:26:12,935 --> 01:26:14,670
Let me tell you something.

1297
01:26:14,737 --> 01:26:18,073
This school is the reason he's doing
as well as he is.

1298
01:26:18,140 --> 01:26:20,743
But to keep him in
a school setting--

1299
01:26:20,809 --> 01:26:24,213
You take him out of this school,
you may as well take his life.

1300
01:26:25,981 --> 01:26:27,983
I've compiled
a list of care agencies.

1301
01:26:28,050 --> 01:26:30,018
Oh, I'll bet you have.

1302
01:26:53,509 --> 01:26:56,612
Yes,
ma'am, I will take care of it
personally.

1303
01:26:56,679 --> 01:26:58,614
Yes, I will.

1304
01:26:58,681 --> 01:26:59,815
Yes, ma'am.

1305
01:27:03,252 --> 01:27:04,620
Yes, ma'am.

1306
01:27:05,220 --> 01:27:06,755
Is that a fact?

1307
01:27:08,557 --> 01:27:10,726
That's some serious money.

1308
01:27:10,793 --> 01:27:13,762
Well, all right. Yes, I will.

1309
01:27:13,829 --> 01:27:15,531
All right, now, you too.

1310
01:27:17,766 --> 01:27:19,735
Hello, Frank.
Harold.

1311
01:27:19,802 --> 01:27:21,770
It's been ages
since you were here.

1312
01:27:21,837 --> 01:27:23,739
Yeah, it sure has been.

1313
01:27:29,912 --> 01:27:31,046
So...

1314
01:27:32,548 --> 01:27:33,882
...what can I do for you?

1315
01:27:33,949 --> 01:27:35,618
What are you trying to do?

1316
01:27:35,684 --> 01:27:37,653
I'm afraid I don't understand.

1317
01:27:37,720 --> 01:27:42,491
Yeah, you do. Calling the school board,
making complaints about Radio.

1318
01:27:42,558 --> 01:27:45,894
This is you getting back at me
for cracking down on your boy.

1319
01:27:45,961 --> 01:27:49,031
Now,
let's not go off making this all personal.

1320
01:27:49,097 --> 01:27:50,599
It is personal.

1321
01:27:50,666 --> 01:27:52,468
IIt's not.
Besides which, if it was...

1322
01:27:52,535 --> 01:27:55,838
...most of the guys at Del and Don's
wouldn't feel the way I do.

1323
01:27:56,705 --> 01:27:58,341
Yeah, what way is that?

1324
01:28:00,275 --> 01:28:03,111
You're one of
the finest coaches
in the upstate.

1325
01:28:03,178 --> 01:28:07,883
And with Johnny and the boys
we got coming
back next year...

1326
01:28:07,950 --> 01:28:11,887
...it's just
better if we do things
the way we used to.

1327
01:28:13,956 --> 01:28:16,992
You just want to be the one
runs Radio out of Hanna.

1328
01:28:22,698 --> 01:28:25,067
At least l know
where you stand.

1329
01:28:27,470 --> 01:28:29,705
Radio. That's the O.

1330
01:28:29,772 --> 01:28:33,075
Big, round circle.
Yeah, you try it now.

1331
01:28:34,410 --> 01:28:37,346
Come on, it's all right.
It's okay.

1332
01:28:37,413 --> 01:28:39,314
There you go, take the pencil.

1333
01:28:41,216 --> 01:28:43,419
You can do it, I know you can.

1334
01:28:45,153 --> 01:28:46,254
That's it.

1335
01:28:58,967 --> 01:28:59,935
There.

1336
01:29:01,169 --> 01:29:04,407
Look at that. You did it.

1337
01:29:04,473 --> 01:29:07,743
Congratulations. Good job.

1338
01:29:07,810 --> 01:29:10,779
Radio right there.
Radio right there.

1339
01:29:17,886 --> 01:29:19,622
Hey, look who's back.

1340
01:29:19,688 --> 01:29:21,390
What's up, Jimmy?

1341
01:29:23,792 --> 01:29:25,828
Johnny, welcome back, man.

1342
01:29:27,095 --> 01:29:28,431
What's this?

1343
01:29:28,497 --> 01:29:30,833
He brought that in
a little while ago.

1344
01:30:02,598 --> 01:30:05,934
Sorry Coach
Jones got mad at you.

1345
01:30:06,001 --> 01:30:07,970
He got real mad.

1346
01:30:12,374 --> 01:30:14,176
Yeah, he did.

1347
01:30:14,242 --> 01:30:17,079
Yeah. Real mad.

1348
01:30:28,356 --> 01:30:29,825
Jackets
playing tough D.

1349
01:30:29,892 --> 01:30:31,960
And there's
a steal by Walker!

1350
01:30:32,027 --> 01:30:33,596
Honeycutt
calling the play

1351
01:30:33,662 --> 01:30:35,363
as the Jackets
walk it up the floor.

1352
01:30:35,430 --> 01:30:36,565
Two!

1353
01:30:37,966 --> 01:30:39,768
Jackson has it
in the corner.

1354
01:30:39,835 --> 01:30:41,704
Finds Clay,
who drives foul line!

1355
01:30:41,770 --> 01:30:43,438
Great pass to
Cunningham.

1356
01:30:43,506 --> 01:30:45,508
Underneath
for an easy 2.

1357
01:30:46,441 --> 01:30:48,110
All right!

1358
01:30:48,176 --> 01:30:50,846
Johnny Clay,
doing it all tonight.

1359
01:30:50,913 --> 01:30:53,949
Down the floor, up the score!
We want 2!

1360
01:30:54,016 --> 01:30:55,751
Now Clay from deep.

1361
01:31:00,355 --> 01:31:01,657
Good!

1362
01:31:08,631 --> 01:31:11,634
Johnny Clay
has 1 7 points.

1363
01:31:11,700 --> 01:31:14,369
And that's the end
of the first half

1364
01:31:14,436 --> 01:31:17,840
with the score:
Hanna, 39, Easley, 34.

1365
01:31:17,906 --> 01:31:21,977
That's a good first half, boys.
That's a good first half.

1366
01:31:23,679 --> 01:31:26,582
You gonna stick around?
Save my seat.

1367
01:31:26,649 --> 01:31:27,950
All right,
bring me a drink, will you?

1368
01:31:28,016 --> 01:31:29,251
Yep.

1369
01:31:31,820 --> 01:31:34,389
I talked to Mr. Tucker
and his colleagues...

1370
01:31:34,456 --> 01:31:36,491
...and we all
agreed that we should

1371
01:31:36,559 --> 01:31:38,627
get together and
have a meeting.

1372
01:31:38,694 --> 01:31:40,896
Well, I don't want
to talk about him.

1373
01:31:43,031 --> 01:31:44,232
Harold.

1374
01:31:46,268 --> 01:31:47,836
I know what you're thinking.

1375
01:31:47,903 --> 01:31:49,838
I thought we were
together on this.

1376
01:31:49,905 --> 01:31:51,907
I must find
the best possible solution.

1377
01:31:51,974 --> 01:31:53,341
It's not about who--

1378
01:31:53,408 --> 01:31:54,777
What is it about?

1379
01:31:58,681 --> 01:32:01,416
You remember asking me
where all this was going?

1380
01:32:02,284 --> 01:32:03,518
Do you?

1381
01:32:04,987 --> 01:32:06,589
I still don't know.

1382
01:32:06,655 --> 01:32:09,091
But I do know this.
I won't sit back and

1383
01:32:09,157 --> 01:32:11,560
let Frank Clay make
the rules on this.

1384
01:32:17,199 --> 01:32:19,835
Clay saves it
off the tip.

1385
01:32:19,902 --> 01:32:21,604
Underneath to Henry.

1386
01:32:21,670 --> 01:32:24,807
Great teamwork!
And the Jackets
go up by 7.

1387
01:32:27,042 --> 01:32:30,345
Clay off the screen.
Jumper! Good!

1388
01:32:35,718 --> 01:32:38,721
Johnny Clay in
the zone now.

1389
01:32:38,787 --> 01:32:40,756
Easley working
the ball upcourt.

1390
01:32:40,823 --> 01:32:43,058
And Clay
with the steal.

1391
01:32:43,125 --> 01:32:47,062
Great pass by Clay to Greer
for the easy 2.

1392
01:32:47,129 --> 01:32:50,699
And the Jackets
are running away
with this one.

1393
01:32:55,771 --> 01:32:58,774
Feels good, don't it?
Feels real good.

1394
01:32:58,841 --> 01:33:01,376
Settle down,
settle down, settle down.

1395
01:33:01,443 --> 01:33:04,579
Now, I've coached a lot of basketball
over the years.

1396
01:33:04,647 --> 01:33:08,050
But I've never had a team play better
than you all did tonight.

1397
01:33:11,153 --> 01:33:13,856
Johnny Clay,
it's nice having you back.

1398
01:33:13,922 --> 01:33:15,791
It's good to be back.
Yeah, it is.

1399
01:33:15,858 --> 01:33:17,259
Good. Good.

1400
01:33:17,325 --> 01:33:19,161
We're still in
this race, so rest up

1401
01:33:19,227 --> 01:33:21,163
tomorrow.
We'll hit it hard Monday.

1402
01:33:21,229 --> 01:33:23,165
All right? Get some sleep.

1403
01:33:25,100 --> 01:33:26,168
Play him, you got a shot.

1404
01:33:26,234 --> 01:33:27,402
Believe it.

1405
01:33:27,469 --> 01:33:28,671
There's my boy.

1406
01:33:28,737 --> 01:33:30,138
Always a pleasure to see you.

1407
01:33:30,205 --> 01:33:32,274
Thirty-two.
Good game, son.

1408
01:33:32,340 --> 01:33:34,109
What's with all the passing?

1409
01:33:34,176 --> 01:33:37,646
With the defense they were playing,
you could have gone for 50.

1410
01:33:37,713 --> 01:33:40,548
You gotta take advantage
of these chances, son.

1411
01:33:40,615 --> 01:33:42,350
See you, Radio.
Bye, everybody.

1412
01:33:42,417 --> 01:33:44,486
Bye, Johnny. Bye, now.
See you later.

1413
01:33:44,552 --> 01:33:46,021
What's that?

1414
01:33:48,857 --> 01:33:50,726
It's nothing.

1415
01:33:50,793 --> 01:33:55,297
Look, son, we got a whole lot
to look forward to next year.

1416
01:33:55,363 --> 01:33:57,399
And I don't want
anything or anyone

1417
01:33:57,465 --> 01:33:59,601
getting in the way.
You understand?

1418
01:34:01,136 --> 01:34:03,906
Radio's not the one getting
in the way, Dad.

1419
01:34:11,146 --> 01:34:16,218
That Frank, he's just scared
you got it in for his son, is all.

1420
01:34:16,284 --> 01:34:18,721
When Gloria was a baby,
I never left her alone.

1421
01:34:18,787 --> 01:34:22,324
Wherever I went,
I made sure
Edith stayed with her.

1422
01:34:23,625 --> 01:34:26,194
I forgot to tell
you Honeycutt called.

1423
01:34:26,261 --> 01:34:28,530
Yeah,
some of the parents asked for

1424
01:34:28,596 --> 01:34:30,833
a meeting with
Lou on Sunday night.

1425
01:34:32,067 --> 01:34:33,435
Just Lou?

1426
01:34:33,501 --> 01:34:35,470
Yeah, I don't think
they're interested

1427
01:34:35,537 --> 01:34:37,472
in your side of things,
do you?

1428
01:34:38,073 --> 01:34:39,607
No, I guess not.

1429
01:34:42,845 --> 01:34:45,180
What the hell kind
of a father--?

1430
01:34:45,247 --> 01:34:48,316
What the hell kind of a father
are you?

1431
01:34:48,383 --> 01:34:51,987
Hell. Maybe the whole thing's
just a big mistake.

1432
01:34:52,054 --> 01:34:55,791
Radio would've been better off
if we'd just gotten him some help.

1433
01:34:55,858 --> 01:34:59,895
Help? And what you've been
giving him has been...?

1434
01:34:59,962 --> 01:35:02,497
Couldn't have been easy
on you and Mary Helen...

1435
01:35:02,564 --> 01:35:05,367
...me spending all this time
with Radio.

1436
01:35:05,433 --> 01:35:07,269
Harold, wait.

1437
01:35:07,335 --> 01:35:10,973
You can't believe that's been
a mistake, you being with Radio.

1438
01:35:12,941 --> 01:35:14,943
You've been so
great for each other.

1439
01:35:15,010 --> 01:35:17,112
Yeah,
well, look where it's got us.

1440
01:35:17,179 --> 01:35:20,715
Where it got you is a school
full of kids that love him.

1441
01:35:20,783 --> 01:35:22,684
And Mary Helen
feels the same way.

1442
01:35:22,751 --> 01:35:26,789
And anything that
Frank can do or say
won't change anything.

1443
01:35:28,690 --> 01:35:31,526
It's never a mistake to care
for someone.

1444
01:35:31,593 --> 01:35:33,796
That's always a good thing.

1445
01:35:35,497 --> 01:35:36,631
Right?

1446
01:35:41,369 --> 01:35:43,305
God bless you.
Thank you, Reverend.

1447
01:35:43,371 --> 01:35:45,808
God bless you.
That was quite a sermon.

1448
01:35:45,874 --> 01:35:47,810
Indeed. Praise the Lord.

1449
01:35:49,044 --> 01:35:50,112
God bless you, Radio.

1450
01:35:50,178 --> 01:35:51,313
Praise the Lord.

1451
01:35:51,379 --> 01:35:52,747
Praise the Lord.
Coach.

1452
01:35:52,815 --> 01:35:54,549
I love that sermon.
I like that.

1453
01:35:54,616 --> 01:35:56,284
All hands are
Jesus' hands

1454
01:35:56,351 --> 01:35:59,754
I like that.
I like the way everybody singing.

1455
01:35:59,822 --> 01:36:02,958
Yeah, that was a nice service.
A nice service.

1456
01:36:03,025 --> 01:36:07,062
I need to talk to you
about a little something here.

1457
01:36:07,129 --> 01:36:10,799
You remember telling me
about being in 1 1 th grade?

1458
01:36:10,866 --> 01:36:14,302
You talking about Mrs.
Winniver. Yeah, I like Mrs. Winniver.

1459
01:36:14,369 --> 01:36:18,440
There's been some talk about
maybe you going
on to 1 2th grade.

1460
01:36:18,506 --> 01:36:22,144
That'd be something,
wouldn't it?
You know, have you graduate.

1461
01:36:23,745 --> 01:36:25,380
Radio, listen to me.

1462
01:36:25,447 --> 01:36:27,415
Put your-- Take your radio d--

1463
01:36:27,482 --> 01:36:30,986
Radio, put your radio down.
Look at me. Look at me.

1464
01:36:31,053 --> 01:36:33,021
There's nothing
wrong with moving on.

1465
01:36:33,088 --> 01:36:35,323
Everybody gets
to it eventually.

1466
01:36:35,390 --> 01:36:40,362
No. No, I like  the 11th grade.
I like the 1 1 th grade.

1467
01:36:40,428 --> 01:36:41,796
No. No.

1468
01:36:41,864 --> 01:36:44,532
I do the menu in the morning.

1469
01:36:44,599 --> 01:36:48,070
I say, ''We're gonna have
hamburgers and mashed potatoes.''

1470
01:36:48,136 --> 01:36:51,539
And then I see people in the hallway,
I say, ''Hey. No running.

1471
01:36:51,606 --> 01:36:54,877
Everybody,
no running.'' Everybody
know that's Radio. I'm there.

1472
01:36:54,943 --> 01:36:58,146
Everybody like that.
They say, ''Hi, Radio!''

1473
01:36:58,213 --> 01:37:00,082
All right, listen.
We'll talk about it

1474
01:37:00,148 --> 01:37:02,117
when we get
closer to the fall.

1475
01:37:02,184 --> 01:37:04,887
Let's not worry
about it right now.

1476
01:37:04,953 --> 01:37:07,856
Radio like the fall.
That's when football come.

1477
01:37:07,923 --> 01:37:11,393
It's football. We'll exercise,
and everybody have T-shirts on.

1478
01:37:11,459 --> 01:37:15,497
And Coach Honeycutt, he be,
''Let's see some Hanna spirit!''

1479
01:37:15,563 --> 01:37:18,566
Yeah. Hey, coach, you say,
''Let's get the quarterback.''

1480
01:37:18,633 --> 01:37:22,337
And Radio, he defense coach.
I'll be defense coach.

1481
01:37:22,404 --> 01:37:24,772
That's right.
We'll go all the way.

1482
01:37:24,839 --> 01:37:26,508
That's right, Radio.

1483
01:37:26,574 --> 01:37:28,343
We gonna go all of the way.

1484
01:37:28,410 --> 01:37:31,046
Because we got the spirit.

1485
01:37:38,853 --> 01:37:42,857
We gonna go all the way.
We gonna go all the way.

1486
01:37:44,592 --> 01:37:48,330
This man is a disruptive force
in our community...

1487
01:37:48,396 --> 01:37:51,066
...and represents a threat
to our students.

1488
01:37:51,900 --> 01:37:53,268
Thank you, Mr. Clay.

1489
01:37:53,335 --> 01:37:57,805
Okay, Okay. I understand how
some of you might be feeling.

1490
01:37:57,872 --> 01:38:00,242
All I am asking is
that if we decide

1491
01:38:00,308 --> 01:38:02,777
that there's no
other way around this...

1492
01:38:02,844 --> 01:38:05,513
...that we dole
out as little hurt as possible.

1493
01:38:05,580 --> 01:38:08,616
Fine.
Honeycutt, is there anything
you'd like to add?

1494
01:38:14,222 --> 01:38:15,690
Evening, Del. Don.

1495
01:38:15,757 --> 01:38:17,292
Harold.

1496
01:38:17,359 --> 01:38:18,526
Evening, everyone.

1497
01:38:18,593 --> 01:38:19,694
Evening.

1498
01:38:22,630 --> 01:38:24,632
Hi, Lou.

1499
01:38:24,699 --> 01:38:26,801
I'm good. I'm good.
How you doing?

1500
01:38:26,868 --> 01:38:27,869
How are you?

1501
01:38:27,936 --> 01:38:28,870
Good.

1502
01:38:29,604 --> 01:38:32,740
I was gonna call you.

1503
01:38:32,807 --> 01:38:34,576
You got a crowded
shop tonight, Del.

1504
01:38:34,642 --> 01:38:36,511
Yeah, coach.

1505
01:38:36,578 --> 01:38:40,382
I think y'all know my wife, Linda,
and my daughter, Mary Helen.

1506
01:38:42,350 --> 01:38:44,886
Evening, ma'am.
Evening.

1507
01:38:44,953 --> 01:38:49,157
Well, I had a talk with Radio
this morning.

1508
01:38:49,224 --> 01:38:51,659
I told him,
in not so many words, that

1509
01:38:51,726 --> 01:38:54,963
we might be
looking at some changes.

1510
01:38:55,030 --> 01:38:57,465
It didn't take long to see
the more I talked...

1511
01:38:57,532 --> 01:39:00,602
...the more he
didn't understand me.

1512
01:39:00,668 --> 01:39:02,904
We got a lot of
that going on around.

1513
01:39:08,843 --> 01:39:11,279
When I was playing,
I had a coach...

1514
01:39:11,346 --> 01:39:14,882
...he used to tell me to keep
my priorities straight.

1515
01:39:14,949 --> 01:39:17,452
He'd say,
''Son, you figure out what's
important.

1516
01:39:17,519 --> 01:39:19,887
You push
everything else aside.''

1517
01:39:24,492 --> 01:39:26,194
I love football.

1518
01:39:28,163 --> 01:39:29,964
I love everything about it.

1519
01:39:31,633 --> 01:39:34,102
I love Friday nights when
you look for a win...

1520
01:39:34,169 --> 01:39:36,771
...and Saturday morning
when you found one.

1521
01:39:41,409 --> 01:39:44,679
But that's not
what's important
right now.

1522
01:39:46,648 --> 01:39:50,018
We got ourselves a young man
we're not thinking about.

1523
01:39:52,054 --> 01:39:55,523
The same young man who could
hardly talk when we first met him...

1524
01:39:55,590 --> 01:39:58,760
...and now he's making
announcements over the loudspeaker.

1525
01:40:00,862 --> 01:40:04,066
Same young man who got himself
a football letter last fall...

1526
01:40:04,132 --> 01:40:07,269
...but never wears it, because
he can't afford a jacket.

1527
01:40:10,472 --> 01:40:12,474
Now we're asking him to leave.

1528
01:40:12,540 --> 01:40:14,042
Harold, we are not asking--

1529
01:40:14,109 --> 01:40:15,843
The man's not done, Frank.

1530
01:40:19,081 --> 01:40:22,584
I know some of you don't know
or don't care...

1531
01:40:22,650 --> 01:40:26,254
...about all that Radio's learned
over these past few months.

1532
01:40:28,390 --> 01:40:30,525
Well, the truth is...

1533
01:40:30,592 --> 01:40:33,395
...we're not the ones
who've been teaching Radio.

1534
01:40:35,297 --> 01:40:37,565
Radio's the one
been teaching us.

1535
01:40:40,902 --> 01:40:42,870
The way he treats
us all the time...

1536
01:40:42,937 --> 01:40:44,639
...is the way we
wish we treated

1537
01:40:44,706 --> 01:40:46,741
each other even
part of the time.

1538
01:40:50,078 --> 01:40:52,380
I know something's
gotta happen here.

1539
01:40:52,447 --> 01:40:54,682
I know some
changes gotta be made.

1540
01:40:56,718 --> 01:41:01,156
And I know I can't let what happened
last season happen again.

1541
01:41:05,227 --> 01:41:08,130
So I've decided to step down
as head football coach.

1542
01:41:19,874 --> 01:41:21,809
See what you've done, Frank.

1543
01:41:26,047 --> 01:41:29,251
I'd like to keep teaching,
if that's all right.

1544
01:41:29,317 --> 01:41:33,588
I'll keep an eye on Radio,
make sure he stays out of trouble.

1545
01:41:33,655 --> 01:41:35,557
And I'd like to
spend more time...

1546
01:41:35,623 --> 01:41:38,826
...with a few other folks
I've neglected over the years...

1547
01:41:38,893 --> 01:41:40,995
...while I still
have a chance to.

1548
01:41:44,899 --> 01:41:47,469
Much as I love
this game, it's not

1549
01:41:47,535 --> 01:41:50,071
half as important as
setting that right.

1550
01:41:54,509 --> 01:41:56,511
That was
a pretty good cup, Del.

1551
01:41:58,680 --> 01:42:00,582
Good night.
Thank y'all.

1552
01:42:07,455 --> 01:42:09,324
This what you wanted?

1553
01:42:09,391 --> 01:42:10,858
Is this worth it?

1554
01:42:14,829 --> 01:42:16,431
That was a crazy idea.

1555
01:42:16,498 --> 01:42:18,300
Weren't
expecting that, were you?

1556
01:42:18,366 --> 01:42:21,603
I can't believe you're gonna stop
coaching football.

1557
01:42:28,676 --> 01:42:33,448
Found it. Under the mattress
with everything else.

1558
01:42:33,515 --> 01:42:34,849
All right.

1559
01:42:36,017 --> 01:42:38,820
You look great, Radio.

1560
01:42:38,886 --> 01:42:39,987
Thanks, Mary Helen.

1561
01:42:40,054 --> 01:42:41,956
All right.
I'll see you out there.

1562
01:42:42,023 --> 01:42:43,958
Get your collar down.
There she go.

1563
01:42:44,025 --> 01:42:46,494
You look good, now.
You look really good.

1564
01:42:46,561 --> 01:42:48,330
You know where
we'll be, right?

1565
01:42:48,396 --> 01:42:49,597
All right.

1566
01:42:49,664 --> 01:42:51,366
Do a good job.
I'm awful proud of you.

1567
01:42:51,433 --> 01:42:53,268
Okay, coach.

1568
01:42:53,335 --> 01:42:56,137
Hey, Radio.
There I go.

1569
01:42:56,204 --> 01:42:58,540
Oh,
hey, Johnny, how you doing?

1570
01:42:58,606 --> 01:43:00,442
I heard you got
yourself a letter.

1571
01:43:00,508 --> 01:43:02,477
Yeah, they gave me a letter.

1572
01:43:02,544 --> 01:43:05,980
Me and the boys
thought you might
need something to put it on.

1573
01:43:07,782 --> 01:43:08,850
That for Radio?

1574
01:43:08,916 --> 01:43:09,951
Yeah.

1575
01:43:15,122 --> 01:43:16,358
How you like that one?

1576
01:43:16,424 --> 01:43:17,725
Looks good on you, man.

1577
01:43:17,792 --> 01:43:20,595
Thanks, Johnny.
Thanks, Johnny.

1578
01:43:22,196 --> 01:43:25,066
Hey, congratulations, man...

1579
01:43:26,167 --> 01:43:27,569
...and thanks a lot.

1580
01:43:27,635 --> 01:43:30,204
Patricia Ann Yearwood.

1581
01:43:33,140 --> 01:43:35,377
Thanks, Radio.
You're the best.

1582
01:43:36,311 --> 01:43:37,679
Thank you.

1583
01:43:37,745 --> 01:43:42,284
I would also like to extend
a special thank-you...

1584
01:43:42,350 --> 01:43:45,019
...to our honorary graduate...

1585
01:43:45,086 --> 01:43:48,323
...Mr. James Robert Kennedy.

1586
01:43:53,861 --> 01:43:55,730
Yeah, Radio! All right!

1587
01:43:55,797 --> 01:43:59,934
Who has decided to return
this coming fall...

1588
01:44:00,001 --> 01:44:03,571
...as an 1 1 th-grade student
at Hanna...

1589
01:44:03,638 --> 01:44:06,173
...where he
will be welcome for

1590
01:44:06,240 --> 01:44:08,710
as many such years
as he so chooses.

1591
01:44:13,415 --> 01:44:14,916
You got your
assistant coach back.

1592
01:44:14,982 --> 01:44:16,418
Yes, we did.

1593
01:44:19,354 --> 01:44:21,623
In that moment,
my husband
was prouder...

1594
01:44:21,689 --> 01:44:24,759
...than if his
team had won
a state title.

1595
01:44:29,163 --> 01:44:32,567
Radio was
now officially
a part of Hanna...

1596
01:44:32,634 --> 01:44:35,102
...and a part of
our lives forever.

1597
01:44:38,005 --> 01:44:39,807
So if you're
ever in Anderson on

1598
01:44:39,874 --> 01:44:42,744
a Friday in the fall,
get there early.

1599
01:44:42,810 --> 01:44:45,112
You'll see the man
they call Radio...

1600
01:44:45,179 --> 01:44:48,450
...leading the Yellow Jackets
onto the field.

1601
01:44:48,516 --> 01:44:50,552
Radio's in
his 50s now...

1602
01:44:50,618 --> 01:44:55,122
...and he's the most beloved coach
Hanna's ever had.

1603
01:44:55,189 --> 01:44:57,091
Coach Harold Jones.

1604
01:44:57,158 --> 01:44:58,292
Harold Jones?

1605
01:44:58,360 --> 01:45:00,695
He was recently
inducted into the

1606
01:45:00,762 --> 01:45:03,197
South Carolina
Coaches Hall of Fame.

1607
01:45:03,264 --> 01:45:05,333
He's retired from
teaching but still

1608
01:45:05,400 --> 01:45:07,535
maintains his
special friendship...

1609
01:45:07,602 --> 01:45:10,572
...with Hanna's
favorite 1 1 th-grader.

1610
01:45:20,114 --> 01:45:24,419
Ready? Ready! Set!

1611
01:45:28,956 --> 01:45:30,625
Touchdown!




